(803383, 103, NULL, NULL, 3131, '[TRANSLATE:TE] Which two Bollywood actors made their Telugu film debuts with \"Devara: Part 1\" (2024)?', '3', 'N', 1, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '[TRANSLATE:TE] Devara: Part 1 marked the Telugu debuts of both Saif Ali Khan and Janhvi Kapoor.', NULL, 803183),
(803384, 103, NULL, NULL, 3131, '[TRANSLATE:TE] Which actor starred as Deva in \"Salaar: Part 1 – Ceasefire\" (2023)?', '4', 'N', 1, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '[TRANSLATE:TE] Prabhas played Deva in Salaar: Part 1 – Ceasefire, released in December 2023.', NULL, 803184),
(803385, 103, NULL, NULL, 3131, '[TRANSLATE:TE] Who directed \"Salaar: Part 1 – Ceasefire\" (2023)?', '1', 'N', 1, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '[TRANSLATE:TE] Prashanth Neel, known for the KGF franchise, wrote and directed Salaar: Part 1 – Ceasefire.', NULL, 803185),
(803386, 103, NULL, NULL, 3131, '[TRANSLATE:TE] Which veteran actor played the title role in \"Waltair Veerayya\" (2023)?', '2', 'N', 1, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '[TRANSLATE:TE] Chiranjeevi starred as a smuggler-turned-RAW agent in Waltair Veerayya (2023), alongside Ravi Teja.', NULL, 803186),
(803387, 103, NULL, NULL, 3131, '[TRANSLATE:TE] Nandamuri Balakrishna\'s 2023 film \"Bhagavanth Kesari,\" directed by Anil Ravipudi, won the National Film Award for Best Feature Film in Telugu at which edition of the National Film Awards?', '3', 'N', 1, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '[TRANSLATE:TE] Bhagavanth Kesari won the Best Telugu Feature Film award at the 71st National Film Awards.', NULL, 803187),
(803388, 103, NULL, NULL, 3131, '[TRANSLATE:TE] Who directed \"Veera Simha Reddy\" (2023), starring Nandamuri Balakrishna in a dual role?', '4', 'N', 1, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '[TRANSLATE:TE] Gopichand Malineni directed Veera Simha Reddy, released during Sankranthi 2023.', NULL, 803188),
(803389, 103, NULL, NULL, 3131, '[TRANSLATE:TE] Which actor played the lead role in \"Guntur Kaaram\" (2024)?', '1', 'N', 1, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '[TRANSLATE:TE] Mahesh Babu starred in Guntur Kaaram (2024), released for Sankranthi alongside Sreeleela and Meenakshi Chaudhary.', NULL, 803189),
(803390, 103, NULL, NULL, 3131, '[TRANSLATE:TE] Who directed \"Guntur Kaaram\" (2024), starring Mahesh Babu?', '2', 'N', 1, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '[TRANSLATE:TE] Guntur Kaaram was directed by Trivikram Srinivas, marking his collaboration with Mahesh Babu.', NULL, 803190),
(803391, 103, NULL, NULL, 3131, '[TRANSLATE:TE] Which actor played the lead role in \"Dasara\" (2023), the directorial debut of Srikanth Odela?', '3', 'N', 1, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '[TRANSLATE:TE] Nani played a coal-mine worker in Dasara (2023), the directorial debut of Srikanth Odela.', NULL, 803191),
(803392, 103, NULL, NULL, 3131, '[TRANSLATE:TE] Which composer, best known for Tamil cinema, scored the music for \"Dasara\" (2023)?', '4', 'N', 1, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '[TRANSLATE:TE] Tamil-industry composer Santhosh Narayanan composed the music for Dasara, set in the Singareni coal belt of Telangana.', NULL, 803192),
(803393, 103, NULL, NULL, 3131, '[TRANSLATE:TE] The 2023 sleeper-hit family drama \"Balagam\" marked the directorial debut of which actor-turned-director, who went on to win the Filmfare Award for Best Director – Telugu?', '1', 'N', 1, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '[TRANSLATE:TE] Venu Yeldandi wrote and directed Balagam, a low-budget Telangana family drama that became a major sleeper hit and won him the Filmfare Best Director (Telugu) award.', NULL, 803193),
(803394, 103, NULL, NULL, 3131, '[TRANSLATE:TE] On what date was \"Pushpa 2: The Rule,\" the sequel to Pushpa: The Rise, released in theatres?', '2', 'N', 1, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '[TRANSLATE:TE] Pushpa 2: The Rule, directed by Sukumar, released theatrically worldwide on 5 December 2024.', NULL, 803194),
(803395, 103, NULL, NULL, 3131, '[TRANSLATE:TE] Who played the female lead opposite Allu Arjun in \"Pushpa 2: The Rule\" (2024)?', '3', 'N', 1, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '[TRANSLATE:TE] Rashmika Mandanna reprised her role as Srivalli opposite Allu Arjun in Pushpa 2: The Rule.', NULL, 803195),
(803396, 103, NULL, NULL, 3131, '[TRANSLATE:TE] Which star played the lead role in the 2025 film \"OG\" (They Call Him OG)?', '4', 'N', 1, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '[TRANSLATE:TE] Pawan Kalyan played gangster Ojas Gambheera in OG, released theatrically in September 2025.', NULL, 803196),
(803397, 103, NULL, NULL, 3131, '[TRANSLATE:TE] Who directed Pawan Kalyan\'s 2025 action film \"OG\"?', '1', 'N', 1, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '[TRANSLATE:TE] OG was written and directed by Sujeeth, and released on 25 September 2025.', NULL, 803197),
(803398, 103, NULL, NULL, 3131, '[TRANSLATE:TE] In \"Kuberaa\" (2025), directed by Sekhar Kammula, which actor played a dual role spanning a beggar and a billionaire?', '2', 'N', 1, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '[TRANSLATE:TE] Dhanush played a dual role in Kuberaa (2025), a crime drama also starring Nagarjuna and Rashmika Mandanna.', NULL, 803198),
(803399, 103, NULL, NULL, 3131, '[TRANSLATE:TE] Who directed the 2025 crime drama \"Kuberaa,\" starring Dhanush and Nagarjuna?', '3', 'N', 1, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '[TRANSLATE:TE] Kuberaa was directed by Sekhar Kammula and released in June 2025.', NULL, 803199),
(803400, 103, NULL, NULL, 3131, '[TRANSLATE:TE] Which pair of actors starred together in the 2025 film \"Thandel,\" about a fisherman detained by Pakistani forces?', '4', 'N', 1, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '[TRANSLATE:TE] Thandel, directed by Chandoo Mondeti, starred Naga Chaitanya opposite Sai Pallavi, released in February 2025.', NULL, 803200),
(803501, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Who founded the Maurya Empire in ancient India?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Chandragupta Maurya founded the Maurya Empire around 321 BCE with the guidance of his advisor Chanakya.', NULL, NULL),
(803502, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Who founded the Mughal Empire in India?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Babur defeated Ibrahim Lodi at the First Battle of Panipat in 1526 and founded the Mughal Empire.', NULL, NULL),
(803503, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which Mughal emperor built the Taj Mahal?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Shah Jahan built the Taj Mahal at Agra in memory of his wife Mumtaz Mahal.', NULL, NULL),
(803504, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] In which year did India gain independence from British rule?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'India became independent on 15 August 1947, ending nearly 200 years of British rule.', NULL, NULL),
(803505, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Who was the first Prime Minister of independent India?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Jawaharlal Nehru became India\'s first Prime Minister on 15 August 1947.', NULL, NULL),
(803506, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Who is popularly known as the \'Father of the Nation\' in India?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Mahatma Gandhi led India\'s non-violent freedom struggle and is honoured as the Father of the Nation.', NULL, NULL),
(803507, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Who was the first President of India?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Dr. Rajendra Prasad served as the first President of India from 1950 to 1962.', NULL, NULL),
(803508, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] In which city did the Jallianwala Bagh massacre take place in 1919?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'British troops under General Dyer fired on an unarmed crowd at Jallianwala Bagh in Amritsar in April 1919.', NULL, NULL),
(803509, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Who wrote India\'s national anthem \'Jana Gana Mana\'?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Rabindranath Tagore composed \'Jana Gana Mana\', which was adopted as India\'s national anthem in 1950.', NULL, NULL),
(803510, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Emperor Ashoka belonged to which dynasty?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Ashoka was a ruler of the Maurya dynasty and grandson of its founder, Chandragupta Maurya.', NULL, NULL),
(803511, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] In which year was the Battle of Plassey fought?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Battle of Plassey (1757) saw the British East India Company defeat Nawab Siraj-ud-Daulah, marking the start of British political power in India.', NULL, NULL),
(803512, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] In which year was the Quit India Movement launched?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Mahatma Gandhi launched the Quit India Movement on 8 August 1942, demanding an end to British rule.', NULL, NULL),
(803513, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Who was the last Mughal emperor, exiled by the British after the 1857 revolt?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Bahadur Shah Zafar was the last Mughal emperor; after the 1857 revolt, the British exiled him to Rangoon.', NULL, NULL),
(803514, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] In which year was the Indian National Congress founded?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Indian National Congress was founded in 1885 by A.O. Hume along with other Indian leaders.', NULL, NULL),
(803515, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Who led the Dandi March (Salt Satyagraha) of 1930?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Mahatma Gandhi led the Dandi March in 1930 to protest the British salt tax by producing salt from seawater.', NULL, NULL),
(803516, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Who led and reorganized the Indian National Army (Azad Hind Fauj) in 1943 to fight for India\'s independence?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Subhas Chandra Bose took charge of the Indian National Army in 1943 and led it against British forces during World War II.', NULL, NULL),
(803517, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Who was the last Viceroy of British India and also became the first Governor-General of independent India?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Lord Mountbatten served as the last Viceroy of British India and continued as the first Governor-General of independent India until 1948.', NULL, NULL),
(803518, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] In which year did the Non-Cooperation Movement begin?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Mahatma Gandhi launched the Non-Cooperation Movement in 1920 in response to the Jallianwala Bagh massacre and other grievances.', NULL, NULL),
(803519, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] The ancient centre of learning at Nalanda was primarily patronized by which dynasty?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Nalanda University was founded and mainly patronized by the Gupta rulers, beginning with Kumaragupta I in the 5th century CE.', NULL, NULL),
(803520, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Who is traditionally regarded as the founder of the Gupta Empire?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Sri Gupta is traditionally considered the founder of the Gupta dynasty, though Chandragupta I later expanded it into a major empire.', NULL, NULL),
(803521, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which is the longest river in India?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Ganga, originating in the Himalayas, is the longest river flowing within India.', NULL, NULL),
(803522, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which is the highest mountain peak located within India?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Kangchenjunga, on the Sikkim-Nepal border, is the highest peak entirely within Indian territory; Everest and K2 lie outside India.', NULL, NULL),
(803523, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which is the largest state in India by area?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Rajasthan is India\'s largest state by area, covering much of the Thar Desert.', NULL, NULL),
(803524, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which is the smallest state in India by area?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Goa, on India\'s west coast, is the smallest state in India by geographical area.', NULL, NULL),
(803525, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] The Thar Desert is located mainly in which Indian state?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Thar Desert, also called the Great Indian Desert, lies mostly in the state of Rajasthan.', NULL, NULL),
(803526, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which is the southernmost point of mainland India?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Kanyakumari, at the tip of Tamil Nadu, marks the southernmost point of the Indian mainland.', NULL, NULL),
(803527, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which mountain range forms India\'s northern boundary with China and Nepal?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Himalayas form a natural mountain barrier along India\'s northern frontier.', NULL, NULL),
(803528, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which city is the capital of India?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'New Delhi is the capital of India and seat of the Union Government.', NULL, NULL),
(803529, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which river is commonly called the \'Sorrow of Bihar\' because of its devastating floods?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Kosi River is notorious for changing course and causing severe floods in Bihar, earning it this nickname.', NULL, NULL),
(803530, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which is the largest island territory of India?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Andaman and Nicobar Islands, in the Bay of Bengal, form India\'s largest island union territory.', NULL, NULL),
(803531, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which Indian state has the longest coastline?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Gujarat has India\'s longest coastline among all states, stretching over 1,600 km along the Arabian Sea.', NULL, NULL),
(803532, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] The Tropic of Cancer passes through how many Indian states?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Tropic of Cancer passes through 8 Indian states: Gujarat, Rajasthan, Madhya Pradesh, Chhattisgarh, Jharkhand, West Bengal, Tripura, and Mizoram.', NULL, NULL),
(803533, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which is the largest freshwater lake in India?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Wular Lake in Jammu and Kashmir, formed by the Jhelum River, is the largest freshwater lake in India.', NULL, NULL),
(803534, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] The river Ganga originates from Gomukh, near which glacier?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Ganga (as the Bhagirathi) originates at Gomukh, the snout of the Gangotri glacier in Uttarakhand.', NULL, NULL),
(803535, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which Indian state is known as the \'Spice Garden of India\'?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Kerala is famous for producing spices like pepper, cardamom, and cinnamon, earning it this title.', NULL, NULL),
(803536, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which mountain range runs along India\'s western coast?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Western Ghats run parallel to India\'s western coastline from Gujarat to Kerala.', NULL, NULL),
(803537, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which Indian state shares a border with the maximum number of other Indian states?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Uttar Pradesh borders the largest number of other Indian states, including Uttarakhand, Bihar, Madhya Pradesh, and others.', NULL, NULL),
(803538, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which strait separates India and Sri Lanka?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Palk Strait, along with the Gulf of Mannar, separates the southeastern coast of India from Sri Lanka.', NULL, NULL),
(803539, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] The Radcliffe Line forms the international border between India and which two countries?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Sir Cyril Radcliffe drew the boundary lines during the 1947 Partition that today separate India from both Pakistan and Bangladesh.', NULL, NULL),
(803540, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which Indian state, through which the Tropic of Cancer passes, also has a coastline on the Arabian Sea?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Among the states crossed by the Tropic of Cancer, only Gujarat has a coastline on the Arabian Sea.', NULL, NULL),
(803541, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Who is regarded as the chief architect of the Indian Constitution?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Dr. B.R. Ambedkar chaired the Drafting Committee of the Constituent Assembly and is regarded as the chief architect of the Indian Constitution.', NULL, NULL),
(803542, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] On which date did the Constitution of India come into effect?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Constitution of India came into force on 26 January 1950, celebrated annually as Republic Day.', NULL, NULL),
(803543, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] According to the Preamble, India is a Sovereign, Socialist, Secular, Democratic what?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Preamble describes India as a \'Sovereign Socialist Secular Democratic Republic\'.', NULL, NULL),
(803544, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Who is the constitutional head of state of India?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The President of India is the head of state, while the Prime Minister is the head of government.', NULL, NULL),
(803545, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which part of the Indian Constitution deals with Fundamental Rights?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Part III of the Constitution guarantees the Fundamental Rights to Indian citizens.', NULL, NULL),
(803546, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Who formally appoints the Prime Minister of India?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The President of India formally appoints the Prime Minister, usually the leader of the majority party in the Lok Sabha.', NULL, NULL),
(803547, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] What is the minimum age required to become a member of the Lok Sabha?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'A candidate must be at least 25 years old to contest and become a member of the Lok Sabha.', NULL, NULL),
(803548, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which house of the Indian Parliament is known as the \'House of the People\'?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Lok Sabha, whose members are directly elected by the people, is called the House of the People.', NULL, NULL),
(803549, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Who is the head of the Indian judiciary?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Chief Justice of India heads the Supreme Court and the Indian judiciary.', NULL, NULL),
(803550, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which form of government does India follow?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'India follows a parliamentary system of government, modelled largely on the British system.', NULL, NULL),
(803551, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] How many Fundamental Duties are currently listed in the Indian Constitution?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Ten Fundamental Duties were added by the 42nd Amendment (1976), and an 11th was added by the 86th Amendment (2002), making 11 in total.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `questions` (`QuestionId`, `SubjectInfoId`, `ChapterInfoId`, `CaseStudyId`, `ExamInfoId`, `QuestionDesc`, `CorrectAnswer`, `ImageInd`, `NumofImages`, `ImageLoc`, `OperatorInd`, `Complexity`, `IsActive`, `IsDeleted`, `DeletedAt`, `DeletedBy`, `QuestionType`, `ExpectedAnswerCount`, `Explanation`, `LinkedFromQuestionId`, `TranslatedFromQuestionId`) VALUES
(803552, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] The Fundamental Rights in the Indian Constitution were largely inspired by the constitution of which country?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'India\'s Fundamental Rights draw heavily on the Bill of Rights in the United States Constitution.', NULL, NULL),
(803553, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which Article of the Indian Constitution abolishes untouchability?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Article 17 of the Constitution abolishes untouchability and forbids its practice in any form.', NULL, NULL),
(803554, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] What is the normal term of office of the President of India?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The President of India is elected for a term of five years and is eligible for re-election.', NULL, NULL),
(803555, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Who was the first Speaker of the Lok Sabha?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'G. V. Mavalankar served as the first Speaker of the Lok Sabha, from 1952 to 1956.', NULL, NULL),
(803556, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which constitutional body is responsible for conducting elections in India?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Election Commission of India is an independent constitutional body that conducts elections to Parliament and state legislatures.', NULL, NULL),
(803557, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] The Right to Property was removed from the list of Fundamental Rights and made a legal right by which constitutional amendment?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The 44th Amendment Act of 1978 removed the Right to Property from Fundamental Rights and made it a legal right under Article 300A.', NULL, NULL),
(803558, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which schedule of the Indian Constitution deals with the distribution of powers between the Union and the States?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Seventh Schedule contains the Union List, State List, and Concurrent List, dividing legislative powers between the Centre and States.', NULL, NULL),
(803559, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] The Directive Principles of State Policy in the Indian Constitution were borrowed from the constitution of which country?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The concept of Directive Principles of State Policy was adopted from the Irish Constitution.', NULL, NULL),
(803560, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which constitutional amendment is often referred to as the \'Mini Constitution\' of India due to its wide-ranging changes?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The 42nd Amendment Act of 1976 made extensive changes to the Constitution, earning it the nickname \'Mini Constitution\'.', NULL, NULL),
(803561, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] In which year was India\'s First Five-Year Plan launched?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'India\'s First Five-Year Plan was launched in 1951, focusing mainly on agriculture and irrigation.', NULL, NULL),
(803562, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] What is the currency of India?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Indian Rupee (INR) is the official currency of India.', NULL, NULL),
(803563, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which organization is responsible for issuing currency notes in India?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Reserve Bank of India (RBI), the country\'s central bank, has the sole authority to issue currency notes.', NULL, NULL),
(803564, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] What does GST stand for?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'GST stands for Goods and Services Tax, a unified indirect tax implemented across India.', NULL, NULL),
(803565, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Who presents the Union Budget of India in Parliament?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Union Budget is presented in Parliament each year by the Union Finance Minister.', NULL, NULL),
(803566, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] What does GDP stand for?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'GDP, or Gross Domestic Product, measures the total value of goods and services produced within a country in a given period.', NULL, NULL),
(803567, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which scheme, launched in 2014, aims at financial inclusion by opening bank accounts for the poor?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Pradhan Mantri Jan Dhan Yojana, launched in 2014, promotes financial inclusion through basic bank accounts for all households.', NULL, NULL),
(803568, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which is the central bank of India?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) functions as India\'s central bank, regulating monetary policy and the banking system.', NULL, NULL),
(803569, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which government scheme guarantees 100 days of wage employment to rural households?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Act (MGNREGA) guarantees 100 days of paid employment to rural households.', NULL, NULL),
(803570, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] In which year was GST implemented across India?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Goods and Services Tax (GST) was implemented in India on 1 July 2017.', NULL, NULL),
(803571, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which body replaced the Planning Commission of India in 2015?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'NITI Aayog (National Institution for Transforming India) replaced the Planning Commission in January 2015.', NULL, NULL),
(803572, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] In which year was the Reserve Bank of India established?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Reserve Bank of India was established on 1 April 1935 under the Reserve Bank of India Act, 1934.', NULL, NULL),
(803573, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which Five-Year Plan is closely associated with the \'Garibi Hatao\' (Remove Poverty) slogan and objective?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Fifth Five-Year Plan (1974-79) incorporated the \'Garibi Hatao\' objective popularized during Indira Gandhi\'s tenure.', NULL, NULL),
(803574, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] The Pradhan Mantri Ujjwala Yojana primarily aims to provide what to poor rural households?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Pradhan Mantri Ujjwala Yojana provides free LPG connections to women from below-poverty-line households to reduce reliance on unclean cooking fuels.', NULL, NULL),
(803575, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] In economics, what does the term \'inflation\' refer to?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Inflation refers to a sustained increase in the general price level, which reduces the purchasing power of money.', NULL, NULL),
(803576, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Income Tax in India is an example of which type of tax?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Income Tax is paid directly by individuals and entities on their income, making it a direct tax.', NULL, NULL),
(803577, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] The Goods and Services Tax (GST) in India is an example of what kind of tax?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'GST is levied on the supply of goods and services and is ultimately borne by the consumer, making it an indirect tax.', NULL, NULL),
(803578, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] What does \'fiscal deficit\' refer to in the Union Budget?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Fiscal deficit is the difference between the government\'s total expenditure and its total revenue receipts, excluding money raised through borrowings.', NULL, NULL),
(803579, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which period in India\'s economic planning history is referred to as the \'Plan Holiday\', when annual plans replaced a Five-Year Plan?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Due to war and drought, India observed a \'Plan Holiday\' from 1966 to 1969, using annual plans between the Third and Fourth Five-Year Plans.', NULL, NULL),
(803580, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which economist, regarded as the architect of India\'s 1991 economic liberalization reforms, later became Prime Minister of India?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'As Finance Minister in 1991, Dr. Manmohan Singh spearheaded India\'s landmark economic liberalization reforms; he later served as Prime Minister from 2004 to 2014.', NULL, NULL),
(803581, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] India\'s Chandrayaan-3 mission successfully landed near which region of the Moon in August 2023?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Chandrayaan-3 made a historic soft landing near the Moon\'s south pole region on 23 August 2023.', NULL, NULL),
(803582, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] The Statue of Unity, the world\'s tallest statue, is dedicated to which Indian leader?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Statue of Unity honours Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel, India\'s first Deputy Prime Minister and Home Minister.', NULL, NULL),
(803583, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] In which Indian state is the Statue of Unity located?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Statue of Unity stands on the Narmada River in Gujarat, near the Sardar Sarovar Dam.', NULL, NULL),
(803584, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] India hosted the G20 Summit in which city in 2023?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'India hosted the G20 Leaders\' Summit in New Delhi in September 2023 during its G20 presidency.', NULL, NULL),
(803585, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which Indian space mission made India the first country to land near the Moon\'s south pole?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Chandrayaan-3\'s successful landing in August 2023 made India the first country to land near the Moon\'s south pole.', NULL, NULL),
(803586, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] What is the name of India\'s first dedicated mission to study the Sun?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Aditya-L1, launched in 2023, is India\'s first space-based mission to observe the Sun.', NULL, NULL),
(803587, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which Indian city hosted the final of the 2023 ICC Cricket World Cup?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The 2023 Cricket World Cup final was held at the Narendra Modi Stadium in Ahmedabad.', NULL, NULL),
(803588, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Article 370, which granted special status to Jammu and Kashmir, was abrogated in which year?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Indian Parliament abrogated the special status granted under Article 370 in August 2019.', NULL, NULL),
(803589, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] India\'s new Parliament building was inaugurated in which year?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The new Parliament building in New Delhi was inaugurated on 28 May 2023.', NULL, NULL),
(803590, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] The Pran Pratishtha (consecration) ceremony of the Ram Mandir at Ayodhya was held in which year?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The consecration ceremony of the Ram Mandir at Ayodhya took place on 22 January 2024.', NULL, NULL),
(803591, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Following the reorganization of 2019, which former state was converted into the Union Territories of Jammu & Kashmir and Ladakh?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'In 2019, the state of Jammu and Kashmir was reorganized into two Union Territories: Jammu & Kashmir and Ladakh.', NULL, NULL),
(803592, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] What is the name of India\'s first indigenously built aircraft carrier, commissioned in 2022?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'INS Vikrant, India\'s first indigenously built aircraft carrier, was commissioned into the Navy in September 2022.', NULL, NULL),
(803593, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Who became the first Indian to win an Olympic gold medal in athletics, winning the javelin throw at the Tokyo 2020 Olympics?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Neeraj Chopra won gold in the javelin throw at the Tokyo 2020 Olympics, India\'s first-ever Olympic gold in athletics.', NULL, NULL),
(803594, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] What does UPI, India\'s widely used digital payment system, stand for?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'UPI stands for Unified Payments Interface, a real-time payment system developed by NPCI for instant bank transfers.', NULL, NULL),
(803595, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] India\'s new Parliament building, opened in 2023, is part of a larger redevelopment project in which area of New Delhi?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The new Parliament building is a key structure in the Central Vista redevelopment project in New Delhi.', NULL, NULL),
(803596, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] The \'Har Ghar Tiranga\' campaign encouraged citizens to hoist the national flag as part of celebrations marking how many years of India\'s independence, in 2022?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Har Ghar Tiranga campaign was launched in 2022 as part of \'Azadi Ka Amrit Mahotsav\', marking 75 years of Indian independence.', NULL, NULL),
(803597, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Who became the first Indian woman to win an individual Olympic silver medal in weightlifting, at the Tokyo 2020 Olympics?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Saikhom Mirabai Chanu won silver in the women\'s 49 kg weightlifting event at the Tokyo 2020 Olympics.', NULL, NULL),
(803598, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] In which year did India complete 75 years of independence, celebrated as \'Azadi Ka Amrit Mahotsav\'?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'India marked 75 years of independence in 2022, celebrated nationwide as Azadi Ka Amrit Mahotsav.', NULL, NULL),
(803599, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] What is the name of the lander module of India\'s Chandrayaan-3 mission, which soft-landed on the Moon in 2023?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Chandrayaan-3 lander was named \'Vikram\' after Dr. Vikram Sarabhai, the father of the Indian space programme.', NULL, NULL),
(803600, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] What is the name of the rover carried by Chandrayaan-3 that explored the lunar surface in 2023?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Chandrayaan-3 rover, named \'Pragyan\' (meaning wisdom), explored the Moon\'s south polar region after landing.', NULL, NULL),
(803601, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which sport is associated with the term \'century\', meaning a score of 100 runs by a batsman?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'In cricket, a \'century\' refers to a batsman scoring 100 or more runs in a single innings.', NULL, NULL),
(803602, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] India has traditionally excelled in which team sport, winning 8 Olympic gold medals?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'India has won 8 Olympic gold medals in field hockey, more than any other country.', NULL, NULL),
(803603, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which day is celebrated as Independence Day in India?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'India celebrates Independence Day on 15 August, marking freedom from British rule in 1947.', NULL, NULL),
(803604, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which day is celebrated as Republic Day in India?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Republic Day is celebrated on 26 January, marking the day the Constitution of India came into effect in 1950.', NULL, NULL),
(803605, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Gandhi Jayanti, marking Mahatma Gandhi\'s birth anniversary, is celebrated on which date?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Gandhi Jayanti is observed on 2 October every year to honour the birth anniversary of Mahatma Gandhi.', NULL, NULL),
(803606, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which is the highest civilian award in India?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Bharat Ratna is India\'s highest civilian award, given for exceptional service in any field.', NULL, NULL),
(803607, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Teachers\' Day is celebrated in India on 5 September to mark the birth anniversary of which leader?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Teachers\' Day is celebrated on 5 September, the birthday of Dr. S. Radhakrishnan, India\'s second President and a renowned educator.', NULL, NULL),
(803608, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Children\'s Day is celebrated in India on 14 November to mark the birth anniversary of which leader?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Children\'s Day is observed on 14 November, the birthday of Jawaharlal Nehru, who was fondly known as \'Chacha Nehru\'.', NULL, NULL),
(803609, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] World Environment Day is observed on which date every year?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'World Environment Day is observed globally on 5 June to raise awareness about environmental protection.', NULL, NULL),
(803610, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] The Olympic Games are held once every how many years?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Summer and Winter Olympic Games are each held once every four years.', NULL, NULL),
(803611, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] What is the highest sporting honour for athletes in India, renamed in 2021 after a hockey legend?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'In 2021, the Rajiv Gandhi Khel Ratna Award was renamed the Major Dhyan Chand Khel Ratna Award, India\'s highest sporting honour.', NULL, NULL),
(803612, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] The Dronacharya Award in India is given for excellence in which field?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Dronacharya Award recognizes outstanding coaches who have produced medal-winning sportspersons.', NULL, NULL),
(803613, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] National Sports Day is observed in India on 29 August to mark the birth anniversary of which sportsperson?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'National Sports Day is celebrated on 29 August, the birthday of hockey legend Major Dhyan Chand.', NULL, NULL),
(803614, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] International Yoga Day is observed on which date every year?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'International Yoga Day is observed on 21 June, following its adoption by the United Nations in 2014 on India\'s proposal.', NULL, NULL),
(803615, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which Indian city hosted the first Commonwealth Games ever held in India, in 2010?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'New Delhi hosted the 2010 Commonwealth Games, the first time India hosted this multi-sport event.', NULL, NULL),
(803616, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] In which city is the Nobel Peace Prize awarded every year?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Unlike other Nobel Prizes awarded in Stockholm, the Nobel Peace Prize is awarded in Oslo, Norway.', NULL, NULL),
(803617, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Which Indian sportsperson is popularly known as the \'Flying Sikh\'?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Milkha Singh, a celebrated Indian track athlete, earned the nickname \'Flying Sikh\' for his sprinting achievements.', NULL, NULL),
(803618, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] World Health Day is observed on which date every year?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'World Health Day is observed on 7 April each year, marking the founding of the World Health Organization in 1948.', NULL, NULL),
(803619, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] Who won India\'s first individual Olympic gold medal, in shooting at the 2008 Beijing Olympics?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Abhinav Bindra won gold in the 10m air rifle event at the 2008 Beijing Olympics, India\'s first individual Olympic gold medal.', NULL, NULL),
(803620, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Knowledge] The Padma Awards in India are announced each year on the occasion of which national observance?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Padma Awards are announced annually on the eve of Republic Day (26 January).', NULL, NULL),
(803621, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] What is the SI unit of force?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Force is measured in Newtons (N), named after Sir Isaac Newton; 1 N = 1 kg·m/s².', NULL, NULL),
(803622, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] What is the SI unit of work done?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Work done is measured in Joules (J); 1 Joule equals the work done by a force of 1 Newton moving an object 1 metre.', NULL, NULL),
(803623, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] What is the SI unit of power?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Power, the rate of doing work, is measured in Watts (W); 1 Watt = 1 Joule per second.', NULL, NULL),
(803624, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Newton\'s Third Law of Motion states that:', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Newton\'s Third Law states that every action force is accompanied by an equal and opposite reaction force.', NULL, NULL),
(803625, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] The tendency of a body to resist any change in its state of rest or motion is called:', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Inertia is the natural tendency of an object to resist changes in its state of motion, as described by Newton\'s First Law.', NULL, NULL),
(803626, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] What is the approximate value of acceleration due to gravity near the Earth\'s surface?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The acceleration due to gravity near the Earth\'s surface is approximately 9.8 m/s².', NULL, NULL),
(803627, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] The energy possessed by a body due to its motion is called:', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Kinetic energy is the energy an object possesses because it is moving.', NULL, NULL),
(803628, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] The energy possessed by a body due to its position or height above the ground is called:', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Potential energy is stored energy that depends on an object\'s position, such as its height above the ground.', NULL, NULL),
(803629, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] According to the Law of Conservation of Energy:', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'This fundamental law states that the total energy in an isolated system remains constant; it can only change form.', NULL, NULL),
(803630, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Sound waves cannot travel through:', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Sound requires a material medium to travel and cannot propagate through a vacuum because there are no particles to carry the vibrations.', NULL, NULL),
(803631, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] In which of the following media does sound travel fastest?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Sound travels fastest in solids because their particles are closely packed, allowing vibrations to transfer quickly.', NULL, NULL),
(803632, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] The normal range of hearing for a healthy human ear is approximately:', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Humans can typically hear sound frequencies ranging from about 20 Hz to 20,000 Hz (20 kHz).', NULL, NULL),
(803633, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] The bending of light as it passes from one transparent medium to another is called:', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Refraction is the bending of light as it passes from one medium into another due to a change in speed.', NULL, NULL),
(803634, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] The Law of Reflection states that:', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'When light reflects off a surface, the angle at which it strikes the surface equals the angle at which it bounces off, both measured from the normal.', NULL, NULL),
(803635, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Which type of mirror is commonly used as a rear-view mirror in vehicles?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Convex mirrors are used in vehicles because they provide a wider field of view, helping drivers see more of the area behind them.', NULL, NULL),
(803636, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Which type of mirror is typically used by dentists to see a magnified image of teeth?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Concave mirrors produce magnified images of objects placed close to them, which is useful for dentists examining teeth.', NULL, NULL),
(803637, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] What is the approximate speed of light in a vacuum?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Light travels through a vacuum at approximately 3 x 10^8 m/s, or about 300,000 km/s.', NULL, NULL),
(803638, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] What is the SI unit of pressure?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Pressure is measured in Pascals (Pa), where 1 Pascal equals 1 Newton per square metre.', NULL, NULL),
(803639, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] A simple machine consisting of a rigid bar that pivots around a fixed point is called a:', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'A lever is a rigid bar that rotates around a fixed pivot point called a fulcrum, used to lift loads with less effort.', NULL, NULL),
(803640, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] A body of mass 2 kg is moving with a velocity of 10 m/s. What is its kinetic energy?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Kinetic energy is calculated as ½mv² = ½ × 2 × 10² = 100 Joules.', NULL, NULL),
(803641, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] What is the chemical formula of water?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Water is composed of two hydrogen atoms bonded to one oxygen atom, giving the formula H2O.', NULL, NULL),
(803642, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] What is the common chemical name for table salt?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Table salt is chemically known as sodium chloride, with the formula NaCl.', NULL, NULL),
(803643, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] The atomic number of an element is equal to the number of:', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The atomic number of an element is defined as the number of protons present in the nucleus of an atom.', NULL, NULL),
(803644, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] The smallest particle of an element that retains the chemical properties of that element is called a/an:', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'An atom is the basic building block of matter and the smallest unit of an element that retains its chemical identity.', NULL, NULL),
(803645, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] A substance formed when two or more different elements chemically combine in fixed proportions is called a:', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Compounds are substances made of two or more elements chemically bonded together in a fixed ratio, such as water (H2O).', NULL, NULL),
(803646, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Which gas makes up the largest percentage of the Earth\'s atmosphere?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Nitrogen makes up about 78% of the Earth\'s atmosphere, making it the most abundant atmospheric gas.', NULL, NULL),
(803647, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Which gas is essential for combustion (burning)?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Oxygen supports combustion; a fuel requires oxygen in order to burn.', NULL, NULL),
(803648, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] What is the pH value of pure water at room temperature?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Pure water is neutral, having a pH value of 7 on the pH scale, which ranges from 0 to 14.', NULL, NULL),
(803649, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Acidic substances turn blue litmus paper:', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Acids turn blue litmus paper red, which is a standard test for identifying acidity.', NULL, NULL),
(803650, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Basic (alkaline) substances turn red litmus paper:', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Bases turn red litmus paper blue, a standard test used to identify alkaline substances.', NULL, NULL),
(803651, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] What is the chemical formula of carbon dioxide?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Carbon dioxide consists of one carbon atom bonded to two oxygen atoms, giving the formula CO2.', NULL, NULL),
(803652, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] The rusting of iron is an example of a/an:', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Rusting occurs when iron reacts with oxygen and moisture in the air to form iron oxide, an oxidation reaction.', NULL, NULL),
(803653, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] What is the common name for sodium bicarbonate?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Sodium bicarbonate (NaHCO3) is commonly known as baking soda and is used in cooking and as an antacid.', NULL, NULL),
(803654, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] The chemical symbol \'Fe\' represents which element?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Fe, derived from the Latin word \'ferrum\', is the chemical symbol for iron.', NULL, NULL),
(803655, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] The chemical symbol \'Au\' represents which element?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Au, derived from the Latin word \'aurum\', is the chemical symbol for gold.', NULL, NULL),
(803656, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Noble gases (except helium) generally have how many electrons in their outermost shell?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Most noble gases have a stable, complete outer shell of eight electrons (an octet); helium is the exception, having only two.', NULL, NULL),
(803657, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] The process of separating the components of a liquid mixture based on differences in their boiling points is called:', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Distillation separates liquids with different boiling points by heating the mixture and then condensing the vapours.', NULL, NULL),
(803658, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] The reaction between an acid and a base that produces salt and water is called a:', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'In a neutralisation reaction, an acid reacts with a base to form salt and water.', NULL, NULL),
(803659, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Which subatomic particle carries no electric charge?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Neutrons are electrically neutral particles found in the nucleus of an atom, alongside positively charged protons.', NULL, NULL),
(803660, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] As of recent scientific updates, approximately how many elements are recognised in the modern periodic table?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The modern periodic table currently contains 118 confirmed elements, ranging from hydrogen (atomic number 1) to oganesson (atomic number 118).', NULL, NULL),
(803661, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] What is the largest organ of the human body?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The skin is the largest organ of the human body, covering the entire external surface.', NULL, NULL),
(803662, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] How many chambers does the human heart have?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The human heart has four chambers: two atria and two ventricles.', NULL, NULL),
(803663, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Which organ is primarily responsible for exchanging oxygen and carbon dioxide in the human body?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The lungs are the primary organs of the respiratory system, where oxygen is taken in and carbon dioxide is expelled.', NULL, NULL),
(803664, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Approximately how many bones are present in an adult human body?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'An adult human skeleton typically consists of 206 bones.', NULL, NULL),
(803665, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Which cell organelle is known as the \'powerhouse of the cell\'?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Mitochondria generate most of a cell\'s energy in the form of ATP, earning them the nickname \'powerhouse of the cell\'.', NULL, NULL),
(803666, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Deficiency of which vitamin causes scurvy?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Scurvy, characterised by bleeding gums and fatigue, is caused by a deficiency of Vitamin C.', NULL, NULL),
(803667, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Deficiency of which vitamin causes night blindness?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Vitamin A is essential for good vision, and its deficiency can lead to night blindness.', NULL, NULL),
(803668, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Deficiency of which vitamin causes rickets (weak and deformed bones) in children?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Vitamin D deficiency impairs calcium absorption, leading to weak and deformed bones, a condition called rickets.', NULL, NULL),
(803669, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Malaria is transmitted through the bite of which insect?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Malaria is transmitted through the bite of an infected female Anopheles mosquito, which carries the Plasmodium parasite.', NULL, NULL),
(803670, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Tuberculosis (TB), a bacterial disease, primarily affects which organ?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Tuberculosis is a bacterial infection caused by Mycobacterium tuberculosis that primarily affects the lungs.', NULL, NULL),
(803671, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Which organ is primarily responsible for pumping blood throughout the body?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The heart is a muscular organ that pumps blood through the circulatory system to the entire body.', NULL, NULL),
(803672, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Which blood cells are primarily responsible for fighting infections in the body?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'White blood cells (leukocytes) are part of the immune system and help defend the body against infections.', NULL, NULL),
(803673, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Which blood cells are responsible for carrying oxygen throughout the body?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Red blood cells contain haemoglobin, which binds to oxygen and transports it to tissues throughout the body.', NULL, NULL),
(803674, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] What is the normal average body temperature of a healthy human?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The average normal human body temperature is approximately 37°C, or 98.6°F.', NULL, NULL),
(803675, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Which organ filters waste products from the blood and produces urine?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Kidneys filter blood to remove waste and excess fluids, which are then excreted from the body as urine.', NULL, NULL),
(803676, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Which nutrient is the body\'s primary and quickest source of energy?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Carbohydrates are broken down into glucose, which is the body\'s main and most readily available source of energy.', NULL, NULL),
(803677, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Which nutrient is most essential for the growth and repair of body tissues and muscles?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Proteins provide amino acids that serve as essential building blocks for the growth and repair of body tissues.', NULL, NULL),
(803678, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Goitre, a swelling of the thyroid gland, is caused primarily by a deficiency of which element?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Iodine deficiency impairs the thyroid gland\'s ability to produce hormones, causing it to enlarge, a condition known as goitre.', NULL, NULL),
(803679, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Which blood group is often referred to as the \'universal donor\'?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'O negative blood lacks A, B, and Rh antigens, allowing it to be safely transfused to patients of almost any blood group in emergencies.', NULL, NULL),
(803680, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] How many pairs of chromosomes are typically found in a normal human somatic (body) cell?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'A normal human somatic cell contains 46 chromosomes arranged in 23 pairs, one set inherited from each parent.', NULL, NULL),
(803681, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Which gas is primarily responsible for the greenhouse effect and global warming?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Carbon dioxide traps heat in the atmosphere and is a major contributor to the greenhouse effect and global warming.', NULL, NULL),
(803682, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Which layer of the atmosphere protects the Earth from harmful ultraviolet (UV) radiation?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The ozone layer, located in the stratosphere, absorbs most of the sun\'s harmful UV radiation.', NULL, NULL),
(803683, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] The process by which green plants prepare their own food using sunlight is called:', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Photosynthesis is the process by which plants use sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide to produce glucose and oxygen.', NULL, NULL),
(803684, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] During photosynthesis, plants release which gas as a byproduct?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Photosynthesis produces oxygen as a byproduct, which is released into the atmosphere.', NULL, NULL),
(803685, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Which gas do plants absorb from the atmosphere for photosynthesis?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Plants take in carbon dioxide from the air, using it along with water and sunlight to produce food.', NULL, NULL),
(803686, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Which of the following is a renewable source of energy?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Solar energy is renewable because it is continuously replenished by sunlight, unlike fossil fuels.', NULL, NULL),
(803687, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Which of the following is a non-renewable source of energy?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Coal is a fossil fuel formed over millions of years and cannot be replenished within a human lifetime, making it non-renewable.', NULL, NULL),
(803688, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] A community of living organisms interacting with their physical environment is called a/an:', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'An ecosystem includes all living organisms in an area along with the non-living components of their environment, all interacting together.', NULL, NULL),
(803689, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] On which date is World Environment Day celebrated every year?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'World Environment Day is observed on 5th June every year to raise awareness about environmental protection.', NULL, NULL),
(803690, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Which of the following is NOT one of the standard \'3 Rs\' of waste management?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The standard \'3 Rs\' of waste management are Reduce, Reuse, and Recycle; \'Repair\' is not part of this common set.', NULL, NULL),
(803691, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Which group of chemicals is primarily responsible for the depletion of the ozone layer?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Chlorofluorocarbons (CFCs), once widely used in refrigerants and aerosols, release chlorine atoms that break down ozone molecules.', NULL, NULL),
(803692, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] In an ecosystem, green plants that produce their own food are known as:', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Green plants are called producers because they synthesise their own food through photosynthesis, forming the base of the food chain.', NULL, NULL),
(803693, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Organisms such as fungi and bacteria that break down dead organic matter are called:', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Decomposers break down dead plants and animals, recycling nutrients back into the ecosystem.', NULL, NULL),
(803694, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Rainfall that has become acidic due to pollutants like sulphur dioxide and nitrogen oxides is called:', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Acid rain forms when pollutants such as sulphur dioxide and nitrogen oxides react with water vapour in the atmosphere, lowering the pH of rainfall.', NULL, NULL),
(803695, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] The variety of plant and animal species found in a particular habitat or on Earth is called:', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Biodiversity refers to the variety of life forms, including plants, animals, and microorganisms, present in an ecosystem or on the planet.', NULL, NULL),
(803696, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Excessive growth of algae in water bodies due to nutrient enrichment from fertilizers is known as:', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Eutrophication occurs when excess nutrients, often from fertilizer runoff, cause rapid algal growth that depletes oxygen in water bodies.', NULL, NULL),
(803697, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Besides carbon dioxide, which of the following is also a major greenhouse gas?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Methane is a potent greenhouse gas released from sources such as livestock, landfills, and rice paddies.', NULL, NULL),
(803698, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] The gradual increase in the Earth\'s average surface temperature due to increased greenhouse gases is called:', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Global warming refers to the long-term rise in the Earth\'s average temperature, largely driven by increased greenhouse gas emissions.', NULL, NULL),
(803699, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Which international agreement, adopted in 1997, committed countries to reduce greenhouse gas emissions?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The Kyoto Protocol, adopted in 1997, was an international treaty that set binding targets for industrialised countries to reduce greenhouse gas emissions.', NULL, NULL),
(803700, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General Science] Nitrogen makes up approximately what percentage of the Earth\'s atmosphere?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Nitrogen is the most abundant gas in the atmosphere, constituting approximately 78% of it by volume.', NULL, NULL),
(803701, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Find the sum of the first 20 natural numbers.', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Sum of first n natural numbers = n(n+1)/2 = 20x21/2 = 210.', NULL, NULL),
(803702, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Find the LCM of 12 and 18.', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'LCM(12,18) = 36, since 36 is the smallest number divisible by both 12 and 18.', NULL, NULL),
(803703, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Find the HCF (GCD) of 24 and 36.', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'HCF(24,36) = 12, the largest number dividing both exactly.', NULL, NULL),
(803704, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Which of the following numbers is a prime number: 51, 57, 61, 63?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '61 has no factors other than 1 and itself. The others are composite: 51=3x17, 57=3x19, 63=9x7.', NULL, NULL),
(803705, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] What is the smallest number that must be added to 4523 to make it exactly divisible by 9?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Digit sum of 4523 = 14. Next multiple of 9 after 14 is 18, so add 18-14 = 4.', NULL, NULL),
(803706, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Find the unit digit of 7^95.', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Unit digits of powers of 7 repeat in a cycle of 4: 7,9,3,1. 95 mod 4 = 3, matching the 3rd/th term in the cycle = 3.', NULL, NULL),
(803707, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Find the sum of the first 15 odd natural numbers.', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Sum of first n odd numbers = n^2 = 15^2 = 225.', NULL, NULL),
(803708, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Which of the following numbers is exactly divisible by 11: 2354, 4576, 9999, 8547?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'For divisibility by 11, the difference between the sum of digits at odd and even places must be a multiple of 11. Only 2354 satisfies this.', NULL, NULL),
(803709, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] How many total factors (divisors) does 36 have?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '36 = 2^2 x 3^2, so number of factors = (2+1)x(2+1) = 9.', NULL, NULL),
(803710, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Express 0.375 as a fraction in its lowest terms.', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '0.375 = 375/1000, which simplifies (divide by 125) to 3/8.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `questions` (`QuestionId`, `SubjectInfoId`, `ChapterInfoId`, `CaseStudyId`, `ExamInfoId`, `QuestionDesc`, `CorrectAnswer`, `ImageInd`, `NumofImages`, `ImageLoc`, `OperatorInd`, `Complexity`, `IsActive`, `IsDeleted`, `DeletedAt`, `DeletedBy`, `QuestionType`, `ExpectedAnswerCount`, `Explanation`, `LinkedFromQuestionId`, `TranslatedFromQuestionId`) VALUES
(803711, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] What is the place value of the digit 7 in the number 528734?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'In 528734, the digit 7 is in the hundreds place, so its place value is 7 x 100 = 700.', NULL, NULL),
(803712, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] The product of two numbers is 480 and their HCF is 8. Find their LCM.', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'For any two numbers, Product = HCF x LCM, so LCM = 480/8 = 60.', NULL, NULL),
(803713, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Find the largest 4-digit number that is exactly divisible by 27.', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Dividing 9999 by 27 gives quotient 370 remainder 9. Largest 4-digit multiple = 370 x 27 = 9990.', NULL, NULL),
(803714, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Simplify: 15 + 6 x 4 - 12 / 3 = ?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Following BODMAS: 6x4=24, 12/3=4, so 15+24-4 = 35.', NULL, NULL),
(803715, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Simplify: (12)^2 - (8)^2 = ?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Using a^2-b^2=(a+b)(a-b) = (20)x(4) = 80.', NULL, NULL),
(803716, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Simplify: 3/4 + 2/3 = ?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'LCM of 4 and 3 is 12. 3/4=9/12, 2/3=8/12, sum = 17/12.', NULL, NULL),
(803717, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Simplify: (0.5 x 0.5) + 0.5 = ?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '0.5x0.5=0.25, then 0.25+0.5=0.75.', NULL, NULL),
(803718, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Find the approximate value of 199.8 x 5.02 (round to nearest 10).', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Approximating: 199.8 is close to 200 and 5.02 is close to 5, so 200x5 = 1000.', NULL, NULL),
(803719, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Simplify: [(5+3) x (9-4)] / 8 - 2 = ?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '(5+3)=8, (9-4)=5, 8x5=40, 40/8=5, then 5-2=3.', NULL, NULL),
(803720, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Find the value of sqrt(0.0961).', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '0.31 x 0.31 = 0.0961, so sqrt(0.0961) = 0.31.', NULL, NULL),
(803721, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Simplify: (2/5 of 150) - (1/3 of 90) = ?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '2/5 of 150 = 60, 1/3 of 90 = 30, so 60-30 = 30.', NULL, NULL),
(803722, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Simplify: (2^3 x 3^2) / 6 = ?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '2^3=8, 3^2=9, 8x9=72, 72/6 = 12.', NULL, NULL),
(803723, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Find the value of 999 x 999 using a suitable algebraic identity.', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '999x999 = (1000-1)^2 = 1000000 - 2000 + 1 = 998001.', NULL, NULL),
(803724, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Solve for x: 2x + 5 = 17', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '2x = 17-5 = 12, so x = 12/2 = 6.', NULL, NULL),
(803725, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Solve for x: 3x - 7 = 11', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '3x = 11+7 = 18, so x = 18/3 = 6.', NULL, NULL),
(803726, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] If x + y = 10 and x - y = 4, find the value of x.', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Adding both equations: 2x = 14, so x = 7.', NULL, NULL),
(803727, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Solve for x: 5(x - 2) = 3x + 4', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '5x-10 = 3x+4 -> 2x = 14 -> x = 7.', NULL, NULL),
(803728, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] If 2x = 3y and x + y = 25, find the value of x.', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'From 2x=3y, y=2x/3. Substituting: x + 2x/3 = 25 -> 5x/3=25 -> x=15.', NULL, NULL),
(803729, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Find the larger root of the equation: x^2 - 5x + 6 = 0', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Factorising: (x-2)(x-3)=0, so x=2 or x=3. The larger root is 3.', NULL, NULL),
(803730, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] If a = 3 and b = -2, find the value of a^2 - b^2.', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'a^2=9, b^2=4, so a^2-b^2 = 9-4 = 5.', NULL, NULL),
(803731, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Solve for x: x/3 + x/4 = 7', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'LCM of 3,4 is 12: (4x+3x)/12 = 7 -> 7x/12=7 -> x=12.', NULL, NULL),
(803732, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] The sum of two numbers is 50 and one number exceeds the other by 10. Find the larger number.', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Larger = (Sum+Difference)/2 = (50+10)/2 = 30.', NULL, NULL),
(803733, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Solve for x: 3(x + 2) = 21', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '3x+6=21 -> 3x=15 -> x=5.', NULL, NULL),
(803734, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Find the sum of the roots of the equation: x^2 - 7x + 12 = 0', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'For ax^2+bx+c=0, sum of roots = -b/a = -(-7)/1 = 7.', NULL, NULL),
(803735, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] If x : y = 2 : 3 and x + y = 20, find the value of y.', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'y = [3/(2+3)] x 20 = 12.', NULL, NULL),
(803736, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Find the area of a rectangle with length 10 cm and breadth 6 cm.', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Area of rectangle = length x breadth = 10 x 6 = 60 sq cm.', NULL, NULL),
(803737, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Find the perimeter of a square of side 9 cm.', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Perimeter of square = 4 x side = 4 x 9 = 36 cm.', NULL, NULL),
(803738, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Find the area of a circle of radius 7 cm. (Use pi = 22/7)', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Area = pi r^2 = 22/7 x 7 x 7 = 154 sq cm.', NULL, NULL),
(803739, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Find the area of a triangle with base 12 cm and height 5 cm.', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Area of triangle = 1/2 x base x height = 1/2 x 12 x 5 = 30 sq cm.', NULL, NULL),
(803740, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Find the volume of a cube of side 4 cm.', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Volume of cube = side^3 = 4^3 = 64 cubic cm.', NULL, NULL),
(803741, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Find the circumference of a circle of radius 14 cm. (Use pi = 22/7)', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Circumference = 2 pi r = 2 x 22/7 x 14 = 88 cm.', NULL, NULL),
(803742, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] A right-angled triangle has legs of length 3 cm and 4 cm (hypotenuse 5 cm). Find its area.', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Area of right triangle = 1/2 x base x height = 1/2 x 3 x 4 = 6 sq cm (legs are the base and height).', NULL, NULL),
(803743, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Find the sum of interior angles of a regular hexagon (6 sides).', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Sum of interior angles = (n-2) x 180 = (6-2) x 180 = 720 degrees.', NULL, NULL),
(803744, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Find the volume of a cuboid with length 5 cm, breadth 4 cm and height 3 cm.', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Volume of cuboid = l x b x h = 5 x 4 x 3 = 60 cubic cm.', NULL, NULL),
(803745, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Find the length of the diagonal of a square with side 6 cm.', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Diagonal of a square = side x sqrt(2) = 6√2 cm.', NULL, NULL),
(803746, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Find the area of a trapezium with parallel sides 10 cm and 14 cm, and height 6 cm.', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Area of trapezium = 1/2 x (sum of parallel sides) x height = 1/2 x 24 x 6 = 72 sq cm.', NULL, NULL),
(803747, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Find the total surface area of a cube of side 5 cm.', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Total surface area of cube = 6 x side^2 = 6 x 25 = 150 sq cm.', NULL, NULL),
(803748, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Find the volume of a right circular cylinder with radius 7 cm and height 10 cm. (Use pi = 22/7)', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Volume = pi r^2 h = 22/7 x 7 x 7 x 10 = 1540 cubic cm.', NULL, NULL),
(803749, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] The circumference of a circle is 44 cm. Find its radius. (Use pi = 22/7)', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Circumference = 2 pi r, so r = 44 x 7 / (22x2) = 7 cm.', NULL, NULL),
(803750, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] In a triangle, two of the angles measure 50 degrees and 60 degrees. Find the third angle.', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Sum of angles in a triangle = 180 degrees, so third angle = 180 - 50 - 60 = 70 degrees.', NULL, NULL),
(803751, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Find the value of sin 30 degrees.', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'sin 30 degrees is a standard value equal to 1/2.', NULL, NULL),
(803752, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Find the value of cos 60 degrees.', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'cos 60 degrees is a standard value equal to 1/2.', NULL, NULL),
(803753, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Find the value of tan 45 degrees.', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'tan 45 degrees = sin45/cos45 = (1/√2)/(1/√2) = 1.', NULL, NULL),
(803754, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Simplify: sin^2(theta) + cos^2(theta) = ?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'This is the fundamental trigonometric identity: sin^2(theta)+cos^2(theta)=1 for any angle theta.', NULL, NULL),
(803755, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] If sin(theta) = 1/2 and theta is between 0 and 90 degrees, find theta.', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'sin 30 degrees = 1/2, a standard trigonometric value.', NULL, NULL),
(803756, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Find the value of sin 90 degrees + cos 0 degrees.', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'sin 90 degrees = 1 and cos 0 degrees = 1, so their sum = 1+1 = 2.', NULL, NULL),
(803757, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Find the value of tan 30 degrees.', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'tan 30 degrees = sin30/cos30 = (1/2)/(√3/2) = 1/√3.', NULL, NULL),
(803758, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] A ladder 10 m long leans against a wall making an angle of 60 degrees with the ground. Find the height it reaches on the wall.', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Height = length x sin(60) = 10 x (√3/2) = 5√3 m.', NULL, NULL),
(803759, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Find the value of cosec 45 degrees.', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'cosec 45 degrees = 1/sin45 = 1/(1/√2) = √2.', NULL, NULL),
(803760, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Find the value of cot 45 degrees + tan 45 degrees.', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'cot 45 degrees = 1 and tan 45 degrees = 1, so their sum = 1+1 = 2.', NULL, NULL),
(803761, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Find 25% of 240.', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '25% of 240 = (25/100) x 240 = 60.', NULL, NULL),
(803762, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] What percent is 45 of 180?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Percentage = (45/180) x 100 = 25%.', NULL, NULL),
(803763, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] 20% of a number is 50. Find the number.', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Number = (50 x 100)/20 = 250.', NULL, NULL),
(803764, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Two numbers are in the ratio 3:4. If their sum is 63, find the larger number.', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Larger part = [4/(3+4)] x 63 = 36.', NULL, NULL),
(803765, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Rs 900 is divided among A, B and C in the ratio 2:3:4. Find C\'s share.', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'C\'s share = [4/(2+3+4)] x 900 = Rs 400.', NULL, NULL),
(803766, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] A number increased by 20% becomes 144. Find the original number.', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Original = 144 x 100/(100+20) = 120.', NULL, NULL),
(803767, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] If a : b = 2 : 3 and b : c = 4 : 5, find a : c.', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'a:c = (a/b) x (b/c) = (2/3) x (4/5) = 8/15, so a:c = 8:15.', NULL, NULL),
(803768, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] The price of an article is increased by 25% and then decreased by 20%. Find the net percentage change in price.', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Taking price=100: after 25% increase = 125; after 20% decrease = 125x0.8 = 100. Net change = 0%.', NULL, NULL),
(803769, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] In a class of 40 students, 60% are boys. Find the number of girls.', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Boys = 60% of 40 = 24, so girls = 40-24 = 16.', NULL, NULL),
(803770, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] If x is 150% of y, find the ratio x : y.', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'x = 150% of y = 3y/2, so x:y = 3:2.', NULL, NULL),
(803771, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] A number decreased by 10% equals 90. Find the original number.', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Original x (100-10)/100 = 90 -> Original = 90 x 100/90 = 100.', NULL, NULL),
(803772, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Two numbers are in the ratio 5:7. Their sum is 144. Find the smaller number.', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Smaller part = [5/(5+7)] x 144 = 60.', NULL, NULL),
(803773, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] A shopkeeper buys an article for Rs 200 and sells it for Rs 250. Find his profit percentage.', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Profit = 250-200 = Rs 50. Profit% = (Profit/CP) x 100 = (50/200) x 100 = 25%.', NULL, NULL),
(803774, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] An article bought for Rs 100 is sold at a loss of 10%. Find the selling price.', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Loss = 10% of 100 = Rs 10. SP = CP - Loss = 100-10 = Rs 90.', NULL, NULL),
(803775, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] An article is sold for Rs 460, earning a profit of 15%. Find the cost price.', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'CP = SP x 100/(100+Profit%) = 460 x 100/115 = Rs 400.', NULL, NULL),
(803776, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] The marked price of an item is Rs 500. A discount of 10% is given. Find the selling price.', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Discount = 10% of 500 = Rs 50. SP = MP - Discount = Rs 450.', NULL, NULL),
(803777, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] The profit on an article is 20% of the cost price. If the selling price is Rs 360, find the cost price.', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'SP = CP x (100+20)/100, so CP = 360 x 100/120 = Rs 300.', NULL, NULL),
(803778, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] A man sells two items, each for the same price. He makes a profit of 20% on one and a loss of 20% on the other. Find his overall profit or loss percentage on the whole transaction.', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'When SP is equal and gain%=loss%=x, there is always an overall loss of (x^2)/100% = (20x20)/100 = 4%.', NULL, NULL),
(803779, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] A shopkeeper allows successive discounts of 10% and 20% on an item marked at Rs 1000. Find the final selling price.', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'After first discount: 1000x0.9=900. After second discount: 900x0.8=720. So SP = Rs 720.', NULL, NULL),
(803780, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] The cost price of an item is Rs 750. It is sold at a profit of 12%. Find the selling price.', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'SP = CP x (100+12)/100 = 750 x 112/100 = Rs 840.', NULL, NULL),
(803781, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] If the selling price of an item is 1.2 times its cost price, find the profit percentage.', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'SP = 1.2 x CP means profit = 0.2 x CP = 20% of CP.', NULL, NULL),
(803782, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] A loss of Rs 50 is 10% of the cost price. Find the cost price.', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '10% of CP = Rs 50, so CP = 50 x 100/10 = Rs 500.', NULL, NULL),
(803783, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] The marked price of an article is 25% above its cost price. A discount of 10% is given on the marked price. Find the profit percentage.', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Let CP=100. MP=125. SP after 10% discount = 125x0.9=112.5. Profit% = ((112.5-100)/100)x100 = 12.5%.', NULL, NULL),
(803784, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] A man sells two watches, each for Rs 600. On one he gains 20% and on the other he loses 20%. Find his overall loss in rupees.', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'CP1 = 600x100/120 = Rs 500, CP2 = 600x100/80 = Rs 750. Total CP = Rs 1250, Total SP = Rs 1200. Overall loss = Rs 50.', NULL, NULL),
(803785, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] A car travels at a speed of 60 km/h for 3 hours. Find the distance covered.', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Distance = Speed x Time = 60 x 3 = 180 km.', NULL, NULL),
(803786, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Convert 72 km/h into m/s.', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'To convert km/h to m/s, multiply by 5/18: 72 x 5/18 = 20 m/s.', NULL, NULL),
(803787, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] A bus covers a distance of 150 km at a speed of 50 km/h. Find the time taken.', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Time = Distance/Speed = 150/50 = 3 hours.', NULL, NULL),
(803788, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] A train 100 m long crosses a pole in 10 seconds. Find its speed in km/h.', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Speed = 100/10 = 10 m/s = 10 x 18/5 = 36 km/h.', NULL, NULL),
(803789, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Two towns are 300 km apart. Two trains start simultaneously from each town towards each other at speeds of 40 km/h and 60 km/h. After how many hours will they meet?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Relative speed (approaching) = 40+60 = 100 km/h. Time to meet = 300/100 = 3 hours.', NULL, NULL),
(803790, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] A man covers a certain distance in 5 hours at a speed of 40 km/h. Find the speed required to cover the same distance in 4 hours.', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Distance = 5 x 40 = 200 km. Required speed = 200/4 = 50 km/h.', NULL, NULL),
(803791, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Convert 25 m/s into km/h.', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'To convert m/s to km/h, multiply by 18/5: 25 x 18/5 = 90 km/h.', NULL, NULL),
(803792, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] A car travels 150 km in 3 hours and then 180 km in 2 hours. Find its average speed for the whole journey.', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Average speed = Total distance/Total time = (150+180)/(3+2) = 330/5 = 66 km/h.', NULL, NULL),
(803793, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] A boat\'s speed in still water is 10 km/h and the speed of the stream is 2 km/h. Find the time taken to cover 24 km downstream.', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Downstream speed = 10+2 = 12 km/h. Time = 24/12 = 2 hours.', NULL, NULL),
(803794, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] Find the time taken to cover a distance of 360 km at a speed of 90 km/h.', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Time = Distance/Speed = 360/90 = 4 hours.', NULL, NULL),
(803795, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] A can complete a work in 10 days and B can complete the same work in 15 days. In how many days can they complete the work together?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Combined 1-day work = 1/10 + 1/15 = 1/6. So together they finish in 6 days.', NULL, NULL),
(803796, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] A can complete a work alone in 12 days. If A works alone for 4 days, what fraction of the work is left?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'In 4 days, A completes 4/12 = 1/3 of the work, so the fraction left = 1 - 1/3 = 2/3.', NULL, NULL),
(803797, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] 6 men can complete a work in 10 days. How many days will 15 men take to complete the same work?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Total work = 6 x 10 = 60 man-days. Days for 15 men = 60/15 = 4 days.', NULL, NULL),
(803798, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] A can finish a job alone in 20 days. B is twice as efficient as A. In how many days can B finish the job alone?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'If B is twice as efficient, B takes half the time: 20/2 = 10 days.', NULL, NULL),
(803799, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] A, B and C can complete a work alone in 6, 8 and 12 days respectively. In how many days can they complete the work together?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Combined 1-day work = 1/6+1/8+1/12 = 4/24+3/24+2/24 = 9/24 = 3/8. Time together = 8/3 days.', NULL, NULL),
(803800, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Mathematics] A works twice as fast as B. Working together, they can complete a job in 8 days. In how many days can B alone complete the job?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Let B\'s rate = r, A\'s rate = 2r. Combined rate = 3r = 1/8, so r = 1/24. B alone takes 24 days.', NULL, NULL),
(803801, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] Which of Newton\'s laws of motion is also known as the law of inertia?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Newton\'s First Law states a body continues in its state of rest or uniform motion unless acted upon by an external force, hence called the law of inertia.', NULL, NULL),
(803802, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] A force acts on a body of mass 2 kg producing an acceleration of 3 m/s^2. What is the magnitude of the force?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Using Newton\'s second law, F = ma = 2 kg x 3 m/s^2 = 6 N.', NULL, NULL),
(803803, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] A net force of 20 N is applied to a body of mass 4 kg, initially at rest, on a frictionless surface. What is the body\'s acceleration?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'By Newton\'s second law, a = F/m = 20 N / 4 kg = 5 m/s^2.', NULL, NULL),
(803804, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] A ball of mass 2 kg moving at 3 m/s collides with a stationary ball of mass 1 kg and they stick together after collision. Find their common velocity.', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'By conservation of momentum: m1v1 + m2v2 = (m1+m2)v -> (2x3+1x0)/(2+1) = 2 m/s.', NULL, NULL),
(803805, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] Newton\'s third law states that for every action there is an equal and opposite reaction. These action-reaction forces act on:', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Action and reaction forces always act on two different bodies simultaneously and never cancel each other.', NULL, NULL),
(803806, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] The coefficient of static friction between two surfaces is defined as the ratio of:', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Coefficient of friction (mu) = limiting friction force (f) / normal reaction (N).', NULL, NULL),
(803807, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] A block of mass 5 kg rests on a horizontal surface. If the coefficient of kinetic friction is 0.2, find the frictional force opposing its motion (take g = 9.8 m/s^2).', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Friction force f = mu x N = mu x mg = 0.2 x 5 x 9.8 = 9.8 N.', NULL, NULL),
(803808, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] A body of mass 0.5 kg moves in a circle of radius 2 m with a constant speed of 4 m/s. What is the centripetal force acting on it?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Centripetal force F = mv^2/r = 0.5 x 4^2 / 2 = 4 N, directed towards the centre of the circle.', NULL, NULL),
(803809, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] A force of 50 N acts for 0.2 s on a body of mass 2 kg initially at rest. Find the final velocity of the body.', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Impulse = Ft = change in momentum = mv. So v = Ft/m = (50 x 0.2)/2 = 5 m/s.', NULL, NULL),
(803810, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] The backward recoil experienced by a gun when it fires a bullet is best explained by:', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The total momentum of the gun-bullet system before firing is zero; hence the gun recoils backward with momentum equal and opposite to that of the bullet, by conservation of linear momentum.', NULL, NULL),
(803811, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] A force of 10 N moves a body through a distance of 5 m in the direction of the force. Calculate the work done.', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Work done W = F x d x cos(theta). Since the force and displacement are in the same direction, theta = 0, so W = 10 x 5 = 50 J.', NULL, NULL),
(803812, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] What is the SI unit of work and energy?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Work and energy have the same SI unit, the Joule (J), since work done equals energy transferred.', NULL, NULL),
(803813, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] Calculate the kinetic energy of a body of mass 4 kg moving with a velocity of 3 m/s.', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'KE = (1/2) m v^2 = 0.5 x 4 x 3^2 = 18 J.', NULL, NULL),
(803814, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] Find the gravitational potential energy of a 2 kg object raised to a height of 5 m above the ground (take g = 9.8 m/s^2).', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'PE = mgh = 2 x 9.8 x 5 = 98 J.', NULL, NULL),
(803815, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] A machine does 200 J of work in 4 seconds. What is its power output?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Power P = Work/time = 200/4 = 50 W.', NULL, NULL),
(803816, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] When a body moves in a circular path at constant speed, the work done by the centripetal force on the body is:', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Work done W = Fd cos(theta). Since the centripetal force is always perpendicular to the velocity (displacement direction), theta = 90 degrees, so cos(90) = 0 and W = 0.', NULL, NULL),
(803817, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] The work-energy theorem states that the net work done on a body equals:', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Work-energy theorem: W(net) = KE(final) - KE(initial), i.e., net work done equals the change in kinetic energy of the body.', NULL, NULL),
(803818, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] A block slides down a frictionless incline from a height of 5 m. Using energy conservation, find its speed at the bottom (take g = 9.8 m/s^2).', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'By conservation of energy, mgh = (1/2)mv^2, so v = sqrt(2gh) = sqrt(2 x 9.8 x 5) ≈ 9.9 m/s.', NULL, NULL),
(803819, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] 1 horsepower (HP) is approximately equal to:', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'By definition, 1 horsepower = 746 Watt, a common unit used to rate the power of engines and motors.', NULL, NULL),
(803820, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] A spring with force constant k = 200 N/m is compressed by x = 0.1 m. Calculate the elastic potential energy stored in it.', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Elastic PE stored in a spring = (1/2) k x^2 = 0.5 x 200 x 0.1^2 = 1 J.', NULL, NULL),
(803821, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] According to the first law of thermodynamics, the heat supplied to a system (dQ) equals:', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'First law of thermodynamics: dQ = dU + dW, which is essentially the law of conservation of energy applied to thermodynamic systems.', NULL, NULL),
(803822, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] What is the SI unit of heat energy?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Heat is a form of energy, so its SI unit is the Joule (J), same as work and other forms of energy.', NULL, NULL),
(803823, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] The zeroth law of thermodynamics is the basis for the concept of:', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The zeroth law states that if two systems are each in thermal equilibrium with a third, they are in thermal equilibrium with each other, forming the basis of temperature measurement.', NULL, NULL),
(803824, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] Calculate the heat required to raise the temperature of 2 kg of water by 10 K. (Specific heat capacity of water = 4200 J/kg K)', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Heat required Q = mcΔT = 2 x 4200 x 10 = 84000 J.', NULL, NULL),
(803825, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] A Carnot engine operates between a source at 500 K and a sink at 300 K. Calculate its efficiency.', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Carnot efficiency = 1 - T2/T1 = 1 - 300/500 = 0.4 = 40%.', NULL, NULL),
(803826, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] Which mode of heat transfer does not require a material medium?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Radiation transfers heat via electromagnetic waves and can occur even through vacuum, unlike conduction and convection which need a medium.', NULL, NULL),
(803827, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] In an isothermal process, the temperature of the system remains constant, which implies that:', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'For an ideal gas, internal energy depends only on temperature. In an isothermal process, since temperature is constant, dU = 0, though heat and work can still be exchanged.', NULL, NULL),
(803828, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] A Carnot engine works between temperatures 600 K and 300 K. What is its maximum possible efficiency?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Efficiency = 1 - T2/T1 = 1 - 300/600 = 0.5 = 50%.', NULL, NULL),
(803829, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] Absolute zero temperature on the Celsius scale corresponds to approximately:', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Absolute zero (0 K) is the lowest possible temperature and corresponds to -273.15 °C, where molecular kinetic energy is theoretically minimum.', NULL, NULL),
(803830, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] In an adiabatic process, which of the following is true?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'An adiabatic process is one in which no heat exchange occurs between the system and surroundings, so Q = 0, and any change in internal energy is due to work done.', NULL, NULL),
(803831, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] A wave has a frequency of 50 Hz and a wavelength of 2 m. Calculate its speed.', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Wave speed v = f x lambda = 50 x 2 = 100 m/s.', NULL, NULL),
(803832, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] What is the SI unit of frequency?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Frequency, the number of oscillations per second, is measured in Hertz (Hz), where 1 Hz = 1 cycle/second.', NULL, NULL),
(803833, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] Find the time period of a simple pendulum of length 1 m (take g = 9.8 m/s^2).', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Time period of a simple pendulum T = 2π√(L/g) = 2π√(1/9.8) ≈ 2.01 s.', NULL, NULL),
(803834, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] The relationship between the time period (T) and frequency (f) of a periodic wave is given by:', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Time period is the reciprocal of frequency: T = 1/f, since frequency is the number of cycles per unit time.', NULL, NULL),
(803835, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] In simple harmonic motion (SHM), the angular frequency (omega) is related to the time period (T) by:', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Angular frequency in SHM is defined as omega = 2π/T = 2πf, connecting angular frequency, time period, and frequency.', NULL, NULL),
(803836, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] A block of mass 1 kg is attached to a spring of force constant 100 N/m and executes SHM. Find its angular frequency.', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Angular frequency in SHM for a spring-mass system: omega = √(k/m) = √(100/1) = 10 rad/s.', NULL, NULL),
(803837, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] Sound waves travelling through air are an example of:', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'In sound waves, particles of the medium oscillate parallel to the direction of wave propagation, making them longitudinal waves.', NULL, NULL),
(803838, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] The Doppler effect explains why the apparent frequency of a sound heard by an observer:', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Doppler effect: relative motion between source and observer changes the apparent (perceived) frequency — it increases as the source approaches and decreases as it recedes.', NULL, NULL),
(803839, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] Resonance occurs when a system is made to oscillate at:', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Resonance occurs when the frequency of the external driving force matches the natural frequency of the system, resulting in a large increase in amplitude.', NULL, NULL),
(803840, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] Two tuning forks of frequencies 256 Hz and 260 Hz are sounded together. Calculate the beat frequency heard.', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Beat frequency = |f1 - f2| = |256 - 260| = 4 Hz.', NULL, NULL),
(803841, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] A resistor carries a current of 2 A when connected across a 12 V battery. Calculate its resistance using Ohm\'s law.', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Ohm\'s law: V = IR, so R = V/I = 12/2 = 6 ohm.', NULL, NULL),
(803842, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] What is the SI unit of electrical resistance?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Electrical resistance is measured in Ohm (Ω), defined by Ohm\'s law as R = V/I.', NULL, NULL),
(803843, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] An electrical appliance operates at 220 V and draws a current of 5 A. Calculate the power consumed.', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Electrical power P = VI = 220 x 5 = 1100 W.', NULL, NULL),
(803844, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] Three resistors of 2 ohm, 3 ohm, and 5 ohm are connected in series. Find the equivalent resistance.', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'In series, resistances simply add: R(eq) = R1 + R2 + R3 = 2 + 3 + 5 = 10 ohm.', NULL, NULL),
(803845, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] Two resistors of 4 ohm each are connected in parallel. Find the equivalent resistance.', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'For parallel resistors: 1/R(eq) = 1/R1 + 1/R2 = 1/4 + 1/4 = 1/2, so R(eq) = 2 ohm.', NULL, NULL),
(803846, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] The direction of the magnetic field around a straight current-carrying conductor is given by:', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The right-hand thumb rule states that if the thumb points in the direction of current, the curled fingers show the direction of the magnetic field lines around the conductor.', NULL, NULL),
(803847, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] A charge of 10 C flows through a conductor in 5 seconds. Calculate the electric current.', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Electric current I = Q/t = 10/5 = 2 A.', NULL, NULL),
(803848, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] What is the SI unit of electric charge?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Electric charge is measured in Coulombs (C); 1 Coulomb is the charge transferred by a current of 1 Ampere in 1 second.', NULL, NULL),
(803849, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] A 100 W bulb is used for 3600 seconds (1 hour). Calculate the electrical energy consumed in kWh.', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Energy consumed = Pt = 100 x 3600 = 360000 J. Converting to kWh: 360000 / (3.6x10^6) = 0.1 kWh.', NULL, NULL),
(803850, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] Fleming\'s left-hand rule is used to determine the direction of:', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Fleming\'s left-hand rule: with thumb, forefinger and middle finger mutually perpendicular representing Force, Field and Current respectively, it gives the direction of force (motor effect) on a current-carrying conductor in a magnetic field.', NULL, NULL),
(803851, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] The mirror formula relating object distance (u), image distance (v), and focal length (f) is:', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The mirror formula, applicable to both concave and convex mirrors (with sign convention), is 1/v + 1/u = 1/f.', NULL, NULL),
(803852, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] What is the approximate speed of light in vacuum?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The speed of light in vacuum is a fundamental constant, approximately c = 3 x 10^8 m/s.', NULL, NULL),
(803853, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] An object is placed 30 cm in front of a convex lens of focal length 10 cm. Using the lens formula, find the image distance.', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Lens formula: 1/v - 1/u = 1/f. With u = -30 cm, f = +10 cm: 1/v = 1/10 + 1/(-30) = 1/15, so v = 15 cm.', NULL, NULL),
(803854, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] Refraction of light occurs because light:', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Refraction occurs due to the change in speed of light as it passes from one medium to another, causing it to bend at the interface (frequency remains unchanged).', NULL, NULL),
(803855, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] A ray of light travelling in air strikes a glass surface (refractive index = 1.5) at an angle of incidence of 30 degrees. Find the angle of refraction. (sin 30° = 0.5)', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'By Snell\'s law: n1 sinθ1 = n2 sinθ2 -> sinθ2 = (1 x 0.5)/1.5 = 0.333, so θ2 = sin^-1(0.333) ≈ 19.5 degrees.', NULL, NULL),
(803856, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] Total internal reflection occurs when light travels:', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Total internal reflection occurs when light travelling from a denser to a rarer medium hits the boundary at an angle of incidence greater than the critical angle, causing all light to reflect back.', NULL, NULL),
(803857, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] A convex lens is also known as a __________ lens because it __________ light rays.', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'A convex lens is thicker at the centre than the edges and converges parallel rays of light towards a focal point, hence called a converging lens.', NULL, NULL),
(803858, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] Calculate the critical angle for a glass-air interface if the refractive index of glass is 1.5.', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Critical angle: sinθc = 1/n = 1/1.5 = 0.667, so θc = sin^-1(0.667) ≈ 41.8 degrees.', NULL, NULL),
(803859, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] Calculate the power of a convex lens with a focal length of 0.5 m.', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Power of a lens P = 1/f (in metres) = 1/0.5 = 2 D. It is positive since the lens is convex (converging).', NULL, NULL),
(803860, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Physics] An object is placed at the centre of curvature of a concave mirror of focal length 15 cm (i.e. object distance = 30 cm). Using the mirror formula, determine the nature of the image formed.', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Mirror formula: 1/v + 1/u = 1/f gives v = -30 cm (same as object distance), and magnification m = -v/u = -1, meaning the image is real, inverted, and the same size as the object — formed exactly at the centre of curvature.', NULL, NULL),
(803861, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] Who is credited with the discovery of the electron?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'J.J. Thomson discovered the electron in 1897 through his cathode ray tube experiments, for which he received the Nobel Prize.', NULL, NULL),
(803862, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] Positively charged canal rays (anode rays), which eventually led to the discovery of the proton, were first observed by', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'E. Goldstein discovered canal rays in 1886 while experimenting with a perforated cathode discharge tube; these rays carried positively charged particles.', NULL, NULL),
(803863, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] The atomic number of an element is equal to the number of which particles present in the nucleus of its atom?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Atomic number (Z) is defined as the number of protons found in the nucleus of an atom of that element.', NULL, NULL),
(803864, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] The mass number of an atom is equal to the sum of the number of', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Mass number (A) equals the total count of protons plus neutrons in the nucleus, since electrons contribute negligible mass.', NULL, NULL),
(803865, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] Atoms of the same element having the same atomic number but different mass numbers are called', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Isotopes have identical proton numbers (same element) but differ in neutron number, giving different mass numbers, e.g., Carbon-12 and Carbon-14.', NULL, NULL),
(803866, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] What is the electronic configuration of a sodium atom (atomic number 11)?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Sodium has 11 electrons distributed as 2 in the K shell, 8 in the L shell, and 1 in the M shell.', NULL, NULL),
(803867, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] What is the maximum number of electrons that the second (L) shell of an atom can hold?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Using the 2n-squared rule, for the L shell (n=2), the maximum capacity is 2 x 2^2 = 8 electrons.', NULL, NULL),
(803868, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] The neutron was discovered in 1932 by', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'James Chadwick discovered the neutron in 1932, confirming the existence of a neutral subatomic particle in the nucleus.', NULL, NULL),
(803869, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] Atoms of different elements that have the same mass number but different atomic numbers are called', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Isobars have the same total mass number but differ in the number of protons, e.g., Argon-40 and Calcium-40.', NULL, NULL),
(803870, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] Which quantum number determines the shape of an atomic orbital?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The azimuthal quantum number (l) defines the subshell type (s, p, d, f) and hence the shape of the orbital.', NULL, NULL),
(803871, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] An ionic bond is formed as a result of', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'In ionic bonding, one atom loses electrons to become a cation while another gains them to become an anion; the resulting ions attract each other electrostatically.', NULL, NULL),
(803872, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] The chemical bond present in a hydrogen molecule (H2) is a', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'In H2, each hydrogen atom shares its single electron with the other, forming a single covalent bond.', NULL, NULL),
(803873, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] What type of bond holds sodium and chloride ions together in common salt (NaCl)?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Sodium loses an electron to become Na+ and chlorine gains it to become Cl-; the electrostatic attraction between these ions forms an ionic bond.', NULL, NULL),
(803874, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] What is the valency of magnesium (Mg) in its compounds?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Magnesium has 2 electrons in its outermost shell, which it loses to form Mg2+, giving it a valency of 2.', NULL, NULL),
(803875, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] According to the octet rule, atoms tend to gain, lose, or share electrons so as to have how many electrons in their outermost shell, resembling the nearest noble gas?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The octet rule states that atoms are most stable when their outermost shell contains 8 electrons, similar to noble gas configurations.', NULL, NULL),
(803876, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] The bond formed between hydrogen and oxygen atoms in a water molecule (H2O) is best described as a', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Oxygen is more electronegative than hydrogen, so the shared electron pairs are pulled closer to oxygen, making the O-H bonds polar covalent.', NULL, NULL),
(803877, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] Given that calcium has a valency of 2 and chlorine has a valency of 1, what is the correct chemical formula for calcium chloride?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'To balance the valencies (Ca=2, Cl=1), two chlorine atoms are needed for every calcium atom, giving CaCl2.', NULL, NULL),
(803878, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] A coordinate (dative) covalent bond is formed when', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'In a coordinate bond, such as in the ammonium ion NH4+, one atom (the donor) supplies both electrons of the shared pair while the other atom (the acceptor) supplies none.', NULL, NULL),
(803879, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] Which of the following compounds is held together primarily by covalent bonds?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Methane is formed by sharing of electron pairs between carbon and hydrogen atoms, making it a covalent compound, unlike the ionic compounds NaCl, MgO, and KCl.', NULL, NULL),
(803880, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] According to VSEPR theory, what is the molecular shape of methane (CH4)?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Carbon in CH4 is sp3 hybridized with four bond pairs and no lone pairs, arranging the four C-H bonds symmetrically at 109.5 degrees in a tetrahedral shape.', NULL, NULL),
(803881, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] In the modern periodic table, elements are arranged in order of increasing', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The modern periodic law, based on Moseley\'s work, states that properties of elements are a periodic function of their atomic number.', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `questions` (`QuestionId`, `SubjectInfoId`, `ChapterInfoId`, `CaseStudyId`, `ExamInfoId`, `QuestionDesc`, `CorrectAnswer`, `ImageInd`, `NumofImages`, `ImageLoc`, `OperatorInd`, `Complexity`, `IsActive`, `IsDeleted`, `DeletedAt`, `DeletedBy`, `QuestionType`, `ExpectedAnswerCount`, `Explanation`, `LinkedFromQuestionId`, `TranslatedFromQuestionId`) VALUES
(803882, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] How many periods (horizontal rows) are there in the modern periodic table?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The modern periodic table has 7 periods, numbered 1 through 7, corresponding to the principal energy levels.', NULL, NULL),
(803883, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] How many groups (vertical columns) are there in the modern periodic table?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The modern periodic table has 18 groups, numbered 1 to 18 according to IUPAC convention.', NULL, NULL),
(803884, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] Noble gases such as helium, neon, and argon belong to which group of the periodic table?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Noble gases occupy Group 18 and have completely filled outer electron shells, making them largely unreactive.', NULL, NULL),
(803885, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] Which element is considered the most electronegative element in the periodic table?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Fluorine has the highest electronegativity value (about 3.98 on the Pauling scale) due to its small atomic size and strong pull on bonding electrons.', NULL, NULL),
(803886, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] Elements like lithium, sodium, and potassium, which are highly reactive metals, belong to which group of the periodic table?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Lithium, sodium, and potassium are alkali metals in Group 1, each having a single electron in their outermost shell.', NULL, NULL),
(803887, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] Fluorine, chlorine, bromine, and iodine belong to which group, commonly known as the halogens?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The halogens occupy Group 17 and have seven electrons in their outermost shell, making them highly reactive non-metals.', NULL, NULL),
(803888, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] On moving from left to right across a period in the periodic table, the atomic radius generally', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Across a period, nuclear charge increases while electrons are added to the same shell, pulling electrons closer and decreasing atomic radius.', NULL, NULL),
(803889, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] The chemical symbol \'Na\' represents which element?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The symbol Na comes from the Latin name \'Natrium\' for sodium.', NULL, NULL),
(803890, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] An element has the electronic configuration 2, 8, 7. To which group and period of the periodic table does it belong?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'With 17 electrons arranged in 3 shells and 7 electrons in the outermost shell, the element is chlorine, placed in Period 3 and Group 17.', NULL, NULL),
(803891, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] What is the pH value of pure water at 25 degrees Celsius?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Pure water is neutral, having equal concentrations of H+ and OH- ions, giving it a pH of exactly 7.', NULL, NULL),
(803892, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] A solution having a pH value less than 7 is said to be', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Solutions with pH below 7 have a higher concentration of H+ ions and are classified as acidic.', NULL, NULL),
(803893, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] When blue litmus paper is dipped into an acidic solution, it turns', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Acids turn blue litmus paper red, which is a standard test used to identify acidic solutions.', NULL, NULL),
(803894, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] Which acid is naturally present in human gastric (stomach) juice and aids digestion?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The stomach secretes dilute hydrochloric acid, which activates digestive enzymes and kills harmful bacteria in food.', NULL, NULL),
(803895, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] Milk of magnesia, used as an antacid to treat acidity, mainly contains', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Milk of magnesia is a suspension of magnesium hydroxide, a mild base that neutralizes excess stomach acid.', NULL, NULL),
(803896, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] What is the chemical name of baking soda?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Baking soda is chemically known as sodium bicarbonate (also called sodium hydrogen carbonate), NaHCO3.', NULL, NULL),
(803897, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] Which of the following is classified as a weak acid?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Acetic acid only partially ionizes in water, making it a weak acid, unlike HCl, H2SO4, and HNO3, which are strong acids that ionize almost completely.', NULL, NULL),
(803898, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] In a neutralization reaction, an acid reacts with a base to produce', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'A neutralization reaction is the general reaction of an acid with a base, forming a salt and water, e.g., HCl + NaOH gives NaCl + H2O.', NULL, NULL),
(803899, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] A solution with pH 3 has how many times the H+ ion concentration compared to a solution with pH 5?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Since pH is a logarithmic scale (pH = -log[H+]), a difference of 2 pH units corresponds to a 10^2 = 100-fold difference in H+ ion concentration.', NULL, NULL),
(803900, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] Ammonium chloride (NH4Cl), formed from a strong acid (HCl) and a weak base (NH4OH), gives an aqueous solution that is', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Salts of a strong acid and a weak base undergo hydrolysis to produce an excess of H+ ions, making their aqueous solutions acidic.', NULL, NULL),
(803901, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] According to the law of conservation of mass, in a balanced chemical equation, the total mass of the', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Matter can neither be created nor destroyed in a chemical reaction, so a correctly balanced equation must have equal mass (and atoms) on both sides.', NULL, NULL),
(803902, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] The rusting of iron, in which iron reacts with oxygen and moisture to form iron oxide, is an example of a/an', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Rusting involves iron losing electrons to oxygen (slow oxidation), forming hydrated iron(III) oxide, so it is classified as an oxidation reaction.', NULL, NULL),
(803903, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] Photosynthesis, in which carbon dioxide and water combine in the presence of sunlight to form glucose and oxygen, is an example of a', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'In photosynthesis, two reactants (carbon dioxide and water) combine to form new products (glucose and oxygen), which fits the definition of a combination reaction.', NULL, NULL),
(803904, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] What are the correct coefficients to balance the equation: N2 + H2 -> NH3?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Balancing nitrogen and hydrogen atoms on both sides requires 1 N2 and 3 H2 to produce 2 NH3, as used in the Haber process.', NULL, NULL),
(803905, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] In the reaction Fe + CuSO4 -> FeSO4 + Cu, iron displaces copper from copper sulfate solution. This is an example of a', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'A more reactive metal (iron) displaces a less reactive metal (copper) from its salt solution, which defines a displacement reaction.', NULL, NULL),
(803906, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] When calcium carbonate (CaCO3) is heated strongly, it breaks down into calcium oxide and carbon dioxide. This is an example of', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Heat causes a single compound (CaCO3) to break down into two simpler substances (CaO and CO2), which is a thermal decomposition reaction.', NULL, NULL),
(803907, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] The combustion of fuels such as LPG or wood, which releases heat and light energy, is classified as a/an', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Combustion reactions release energy in the form of heat and light to the surroundings, making them exothermic.', NULL, NULL),
(803908, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] To balance the combustion equation CH4 + O2 -> CO2 + H2O, what coefficient is needed before O2?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The balanced equation is CH4 + 2O2 -> CO2 + 2H2O, since 2 oxygen molecules are needed to supply 4 oxygen atoms for one CO2 and two H2O molecules.', NULL, NULL),
(803909, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] In the reaction Zn + CuSO4 -> ZnSO4 + Cu, which substance acts as the oxidizing agent?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Cu2+ ions in CuSO4 gain electrons (are reduced) from zinc, so CuSO4 acts as the oxidizing agent, while zinc acts as the reducing agent.', NULL, NULL),
(803910, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Chemistry] The reaction AgNO3 + NaCl -> AgCl (precipitate) + NaNO3, in which a white insoluble precipitate is formed, is best classified as a', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The positive and negative ions of the two reactants exchange partners to form an insoluble salt (AgCl) and a soluble salt (NaNO3), characteristic of a double displacement reaction.', NULL, NULL),
(803911, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] What does CPU stand for?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'CPU (Central Processing Unit) is the brain of the computer that executes instructions.', NULL, NULL),
(803912, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] How many bits make one byte?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'A byte is a standard unit of digital information equal to 8 bits.', NULL, NULL),
(803913, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] Which type of memory loses its data when the computer is switched off?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'RAM (Random Access Memory) is volatile memory, meaning its contents are lost when power is removed.', NULL, NULL),
(803914, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] Which generation of computers used vacuum tubes as their main electronic component?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'First-generation computers (roughly 1940-1956) relied on vacuum tubes, which were large and generated a lot of heat.', NULL, NULL),
(803915, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] The invention of the microprocessor marked the beginning of which generation of computers?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Fourth-generation computers (from around 1971 onward) used microprocessors, which placed an entire CPU on a single chip.', NULL, NULL),
(803916, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] What does ROM stand for?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'ROM (Read Only Memory) is non-volatile memory that typically stores firmware and cannot be easily altered.', NULL, NULL),
(803917, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] Which of the following is an example of system software?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'An operating system manages hardware and software resources and is core system software, unlike application software such as MS Word.', NULL, NULL),
(803918, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] 1 Kilobyte (KB) is equal to how many bytes?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'In standard computer memory notation, 1 KB = 1024 bytes (2 to the power 10 bytes).', NULL, NULL),
(803919, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] Which of the following correctly lists memory units from smallest to largest?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The correct ascending order of memory units is Byte < KB < MB < GB < TB, each roughly 1024 times the previous unit.', NULL, NULL),
(803920, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] Which of the following is an input device?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'A keyboard is used to enter data into the computer, making it an input device, while monitor, printer and speaker are output devices.', NULL, NULL),
(803921, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] Which device is used to convert soft copy into hard copy?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'A printer produces a physical (hard copy) output from digital (soft copy) data.', NULL, NULL),
(803922, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] Which of the following is an example of a pointing input device?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'A mouse is a pointing device used to control the on-screen cursor and select items.', NULL, NULL),
(803923, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] Which device is used to convert a physical document into a digital image?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'A scanner captures an image of a physical document and converts it into digital form for storage or editing.', NULL, NULL),
(803924, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] Which of the following is considered both an input and output device?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'A touchscreen accepts touch input from the user and also displays output, making it both an input and output device.', NULL, NULL),
(803925, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] Which output device is commonly used to produce large-scale drawings such as architectural plans and maps?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'A plotter is a specialized output device that draws high-quality vector graphics, commonly used for engineering and architectural drawings.', NULL, NULL),
(803926, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] Which of the following devices is primarily used for audio input?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'A microphone captures sound and converts it into an electrical/digital signal, making it an audio input device.', NULL, NULL),
(803927, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] A webcam is best classified as which type of device?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'A webcam captures video and images to feed into the computer, so it functions as an input device.', NULL, NULL),
(803928, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] Which keyboard shortcut is used to save a document in MS Word?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Ctrl + S is the standard shortcut to save the current file in most Windows applications, including MS Word.', NULL, NULL),
(803929, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] What is the default file extension for a document saved in Microsoft Word 2007 or later?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Since Word 2007, the default XML-based format uses the .docx extension, replacing the older .doc format.', NULL, NULL),
(803930, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] Which keyboard shortcut is used to copy selected text?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Ctrl + C copies the selected content to the clipboard so it can be pasted elsewhere using Ctrl + V.', NULL, NULL),
(803931, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] In MS Excel, which symbol must be typed first to begin writing a formula in a cell?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Every formula in Excel begins with an equal sign (=), which tells Excel that the cell contains a calculation rather than plain text.', NULL, NULL),
(803932, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] What is the default file extension for a Microsoft Excel workbook saved in Excel 2007 or later?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Since Excel 2007, the default XML-based workbook format uses the .xlsx extension, replacing the older .xls format.', NULL, NULL),
(803933, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] Which Excel function is used to add up a range of numeric values?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The SUM function, e.g. =SUM(A1:A10), adds together all the numbers in the specified range of cells.', NULL, NULL),
(803934, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] Which keyboard shortcut starts a slide show from the beginning in MS PowerPoint?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Pressing F5 in PowerPoint starts the slide show from the first slide; Shift+F5 starts it from the current slide.', NULL, NULL),
(803935, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] What is the default file extension for a PowerPoint presentation saved in PowerPoint 2007 or later?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Since PowerPoint 2007, the default XML-based presentation format uses the .pptx extension, replacing the older .ppt format.', NULL, NULL),
(803936, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] Which keyboard shortcut is used to undo the last action in MS Office applications?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Ctrl + Z reverses (undoes) the most recent action, while Ctrl + Y is commonly used to redo an undone action.', NULL, NULL),
(803937, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] In MS Excel, the intersection of a row and a column is called a?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'A cell is the basic unit of an Excel worksheet, formed where a row and a column intersect, identified by a reference such as A1.', NULL, NULL),
(803938, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] What does URL stand for?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'A URL (Uniform Resource Locator) is the address used to locate a resource, such as a web page, on the internet.', NULL, NULL),
(803939, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] Which of the following is a web browser?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Google Chrome is a web browser used to access and view websites on the internet, unlike the other listed applications.', NULL, NULL),
(803940, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] A network that connects computers within a single building or campus is called a?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'A LAN (Local Area Network) connects computers within a limited area such as an office, building, or campus.', NULL, NULL),
(803941, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] A network that spans a large geographical area, such as connecting cities or countries, is called a?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'A WAN (Wide Area Network) covers a broad geographic area and often connects multiple LANs; the internet itself is the largest WAN.', NULL, NULL),
(803942, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] What is the primary function of an IP address?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'An IP address is a unique numerical label assigned to each device connected to a network, allowing devices to locate and communicate with each other.', NULL, NULL),
(803943, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] Which protocol is primarily used for secure, encrypted communication between a web browser and a website?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'HTTPS (HyperText Transfer Protocol Secure) encrypts data exchanged between the browser and the website, unlike plain HTTP.', NULL, NULL),
(803944, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] In an email, what does BCC stand for?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'BCC (Blind Carbon Copy) sends a copy of an email to a recipient without other recipients being able to see that address.', NULL, NULL),
(803945, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] Which symbol is mandatory in every valid email address?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Every email address contains an @ symbol separating the username from the domain name, e.g. name@example.com.', NULL, NULL),
(803946, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] Which of the following best describes what a modem does?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'A modem (modulator-demodulator) converts digital data from a computer into analog signals for transmission over telephone or cable lines, and vice versa, enabling internet access.', NULL, NULL),
(803947, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] What is a computer virus?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'A computer virus is malicious software designed to spread from one system to another and damage data or system functionality.', NULL, NULL),
(803948, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] What is \'phishing\' in the context of cyber security?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Phishing involves deceptive emails or messages that trick users into revealing sensitive information like passwords or bank details.', NULL, NULL),
(803949, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] Which of the following is considered a strong and safe password practice?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Strong passwords combine varied character types and avoid easily guessable personal information, and should never be reused across accounts or shared.', NULL, NULL),
(803950, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] What is the main function of a firewall in a computer network?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'A firewall acts as a barrier between a trusted internal network and untrusted external networks, filtering traffic to block unauthorized access.', NULL, NULL),
(803951, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] What is the purpose of antivirus software?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Antivirus software scans for, identifies, and removes viruses and other malware to protect a computer system.', NULL, NULL),
(803952, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] What is \'malware\' a general term for?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Malware is an umbrella term covering viruses, worms, trojans, spyware, ransomware, and other harmful software.', NULL, NULL),
(803953, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] What type of malware disguises itself as legitimate software to trick users into installing it?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'A Trojan horse malware appears to be a legitimate or useful program but carries out harmful actions once installed on a system.', NULL, NULL),
(803954, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] What is \'ransomware\' designed to do?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Ransomware encrypts or locks a victim\'s files or system and demands payment (a ransom) to restore access.', NULL, NULL),
(803955, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[Computer Science] Which of the following is a recommended cyber safety practice while using public Wi-Fi?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Public Wi-Fi networks are often unsecured, so avoiding sensitive transactions (like banking) on them reduces the risk of data interception.', NULL, NULL),
(803956, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Identify the abstract noun in the sentence: \'The soldier displayed great courage during the mission.\'', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '\'Courage\' names a quality or idea rather than a physical thing, making it an abstract noun; \'soldier\' and \'mission\' are concrete/common nouns.', NULL, NULL),
(803957, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] How many pronouns are there in the sentence: \'He gave his book to her.\'?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '\'He\', \'his\', and \'her\' are all pronouns, so the sentence contains three pronouns.', NULL, NULL),
(803958, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Identify the adjective in the sentence: \'The brave soldier fought valiantly.\'', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '\'Brave\' describes the noun \'soldier\', so it functions as an adjective; \'valiantly\' is an adverb modifying the verb \'fought\'.', NULL, NULL),
(803959, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Identify the preposition in the sentence: \'The candidates gathered outside the examination hall.\'', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '\'Outside\' shows the relationship between \'gathered\' and \'the examination hall\', indicating position, making it a preposition.', NULL, NULL),
(803960, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Identify the conjunction in the sentence: \'He was tired, but he continued the drill.\'', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '\'But\' joins the two clauses of the sentence while showing contrast, so it functions as a conjunction.', NULL, NULL),
(803961, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Which word is used as a verb in the sentence: \'The Army recruits thousands of soldiers every year.\'?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Although \'recruits\' can be a noun, here it is the main verb of the sentence, meaning \'enlists\', with \'Army\' as its subject.', NULL, NULL),
(803962, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Choose the correct form to complete the sentence: \'She ___ to the market every morning.\'', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'For a habitual action with a third-person singular subject (\'She\'), the simple present tense requires \'goes\'.', NULL, NULL),
(803963, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Choose the correct form to complete the sentence: \'They ___ their training last week.\'', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '\'Last week\' indicates a definite time in the past, so the simple past tense \'completed\' is required.', NULL, NULL),
(803964, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Choose the correct form to complete the sentence: \'The results ___ announced next week.\'', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '\'Next week\' refers to a future time, and the passive voice construction requires the simple future \'will be announced\'.', NULL, NULL),
(803965, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Choose the correct form to complete the sentence: \'By the time the officer arrived, the soldiers ___ already assembled.\'', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'Since the assembling happened before another past action (the officer\'s arrival), the past perfect tense \'had already assembled\' is correct.', NULL, NULL),
(803966, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Choose the grammatically correct sentence.', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '\'Neither of\' is followed by a plural noun but takes a singular verb, so \'has submitted\' is correct.', NULL, NULL),
(803967, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Choose the correct form to complete the sentence: \'If he ___ hard, he would have passed the exam.\'', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'This is a third conditional sentence describing an unreal past situation, which requires \'if + past perfect\' in the if-clause.', NULL, NULL),
(803968, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Choose the correct form to complete the sentence: \'While the soldiers ___ drill practice, it started raining.\'', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'An ongoing past action interrupted by another past event is expressed using the past continuous tense, \'were doing\'.', NULL, NULL),
(803969, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Choose the correct form to complete the sentence: \'By 2030, the Armed Forces ___ modernised most of its equipment.\'', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'An action that will be completed before a specified future time is expressed using the future perfect tense, \'will have modernised\'.', NULL, NULL),
(803970, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Choose the correct one-word substitute: \'A person who loves his country and is ready to defend it.\'', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'A \'patriot\' is someone devoted to and willing to defend their country, unlike a \'traitor\' who betrays it.', NULL, NULL),
(803971, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Choose the correct one-word substitute: \'A place where weapons and ammunition are stored.\'', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'An \'armoury\' is specifically a storage place for weapons, whereas \'barracks\' house soldiers and \'infirmary\' treats the sick.', NULL, NULL),
(803972, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Choose the correct meaning of the idiom \'to face the music\'.', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '\'To face the music\' means accepting criticism or punishment for something one has done, not avoiding it.', NULL, NULL),
(803973, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Choose the correct meaning of the word \'Reconnaissance\'.', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '\'Reconnaissance\' refers to survey or exploration, especially for military purposes, to gather information about enemy positions.', NULL, NULL),
(803974, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Choose the word that is closest in meaning to \'to give up a position, right, or claim formally\'.', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '\'Relinquish\' means to formally give up or surrender something, unlike \'reinforce\' (strengthen) or \'retrieve\' (get back).', NULL, NULL),
(803975, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Choose the correct meaning of the word \'Ubiquitous\'.', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '\'Ubiquitous\' describes something that seems to be present or appear everywhere at once.', NULL, NULL),
(803976, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Choose the word most similar in meaning to \'Brave\'.', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '\'Courageous\' means showing bravery, making it a direct synonym of \'brave\'; the others describe a lack of courage.', NULL, NULL),
(803977, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Choose the word most similar in meaning to \'Rapid\'.', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '\'Swift\' means moving fast, which matches the meaning of \'rapid\'; the other options suggest slowness.', NULL, NULL),
(803978, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Choose the word most similar in meaning to \'Diligent\'.', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '\'Diligent\' describes someone who works hard and carefully, making \'hardworking\' its closest synonym.', NULL, NULL),
(803979, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Choose the word most similar in meaning to \'Concise\'.', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '\'Concise\' means expressed clearly in few words, which matches \'brief\'; \'lengthy\' and \'complicated\' mean the opposite.', NULL, NULL),
(803980, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Choose the word opposite in meaning to \'Victory\'.', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '\'Defeat\' means losing a contest or battle, which is the direct opposite of \'victory\'.', NULL, NULL),
(803981, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Choose the word opposite in meaning to \'Generous\'.', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '\'Stingy\' describes someone unwilling to give or share, which is the opposite of being \'generous\'.', NULL, NULL),
(803982, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Choose the word opposite in meaning to \'Genuine\'.', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '\'Fake\' means not real or authentic, making it the direct antonym of \'genuine\'.', NULL, NULL),
(803983, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Choose the word opposite in meaning to \'Obsolete\'.', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '\'Obsolete\' means no longer in use or outdated, so its opposite is \'modern\', meaning current or up to date.', NULL, NULL),
(803984, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Identify the part of the sentence that contains a grammatical error: \'The team of soldiers (A) / were marching (B) / towards the border (C) / No error (D)\'', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '\'Team\' is a collective noun treated as a singular unit here, so it should take the singular verb \'was marching\', not \'were marching\'.', NULL, NULL),
(803985, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Identify the part of the sentence that contains a grammatical error: \'Each of the candidates (A) / have submitted (B) / their application forms (C) / No error (D)\'', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '\'Each\' is always singular, so the verb should be \'has submitted\', not \'have submitted\'.', NULL, NULL),
(803986, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Identify the part of the sentence that contains a grammatical error: \'Neither the officer nor the soldiers (A) / was aware (B) / of the sudden attack (C) / No error (D)\'', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'When \'neither...nor\' joins subjects of different number, the verb agrees with the nearer subject \'soldiers\' (plural), so it should be \'were aware\'.', NULL, NULL),
(803987, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Identify the part of the sentence that contains a grammatical error: \'She is one of the best clerks (A) / who has worked (B) / in this office for ten years (C) / No error (D)\'', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'In the pattern \'one of the + plural noun + who\', the relative pronoun refers to the plural noun, so the verb should be \'have worked\'.', NULL, NULL),
(803988, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Identify the part of the sentence that contains a grammatical error: \'He is enough intelligent (A) / to solve this problem (B) / without any help (C) / No error (D)\'', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The adverb \'enough\' must follow the adjective it modifies, so the correct phrase is \'intelligent enough\', not \'enough intelligent\'.', NULL, NULL),
(803989, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Identify the part of the sentence that contains a grammatical error: \'Scarcely had the exam begun (A) / than the fire alarm (B) / started ringing loudly (C) / No error (D)\'', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Hard', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, '\'Scarcely\' must be paired with \'when\', not \'than\'; the correct correlative construction is \'scarcely...when\'.', NULL, NULL),
(803990, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Identify the part of the sentence that contains a grammatical error: \'I have visited (A) / the Red Fort (B) / last year (C) / No error (D)\'', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'A definite past time marker such as \'last year\' requires the simple past tense \'visited\', not the present perfect \'have visited\'.', NULL, NULL),
(803991, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Read the passage and answer the question that follows.\r\n\r\nThe Agnipath scheme was introduced by the Indian government to recruit young soldiers, called Agniveers, into the Armed Forces for a period of four years. Candidates between the ages of seventeen and a half and twenty-one are eligible to apply. After rigorous training, Agniveers serve in various roles, including combat and support duties. At the end of their tenure, up to twenty-five percent of them may be selected for permanent enrolment based on performance and organisational requirements. The scheme aims to create a younger, more agile fighting force while also preparing disciplined youth for civilian careers after their service.\r\n\r\nAccording to the passage, what is the age eligibility range for Agnipath scheme applicants?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The passage clearly states that candidates between seventeen and a half and twenty-one years of age are eligible to apply.', NULL, NULL),
(803992, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Read the passage and answer the question that follows.\r\n\r\nThe Agnipath scheme was introduced by the Indian government to recruit young soldiers, called Agniveers, into the Armed Forces for a period of four years. Candidates between the ages of seventeen and a half and twenty-one are eligible to apply. After rigorous training, Agniveers serve in various roles, including combat and support duties. At the end of their tenure, up to twenty-five percent of them may be selected for permanent enrolment based on performance and organisational requirements. The scheme aims to create a younger, more agile fighting force while also preparing disciplined youth for civilian careers after their service.\r\n\r\nWhat percentage of Agniveers may be selected for permanent enrolment, as per the passage?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The passage states that up to twenty-five percent of Agniveers may be selected for permanent enrolment based on performance.', NULL, NULL),
(803993, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Read the passage and answer the question that follows.\r\n\r\nThe Agnipath scheme was introduced by the Indian government to recruit young soldiers, called Agniveers, into the Armed Forces for a period of four years. Candidates between the ages of seventeen and a half and twenty-one are eligible to apply. After rigorous training, Agniveers serve in various roles, including combat and support duties. At the end of their tenure, up to twenty-five percent of them may be selected for permanent enrolment based on performance and organisational requirements. The scheme aims to create a younger, more agile fighting force while also preparing disciplined youth for civilian careers after their service.\r\n\r\nFor how many years do Agniveers initially serve, according to the passage?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The passage mentions that Agniveers are recruited into the Armed Forces for a period of four years.', NULL, NULL),
(803994, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Read the passage and answer the question that follows.\r\n\r\nGood communication skills are essential for every soldier, especially those working in administrative roles such as clerks and store keepers. Clear written and spoken English helps in maintaining accurate records, writing reports, and communicating instructions without confusion. In the Armed Forces, even a small error in a written order can lead to serious consequences. Therefore, recruits are trained not only in weapons handling and physical fitness but also in reading comprehension, grammar, and vocabulary. This combination of skills ensures that every soldier, regardless of his specific duty, can perform his responsibilities efficiently and accurately.\r\n\r\nAccording to the passage, why is clear English important for clerks and store keepers?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The passage states that clear written and spoken English helps maintain accurate records and communicate instructions without confusion.', NULL, NULL),
(803995, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Read the passage and answer the question that follows.\r\n\r\nGood communication skills are essential for every soldier, especially those working in administrative roles such as clerks and store keepers. Clear written and spoken English helps in maintaining accurate records, writing reports, and communicating instructions without confusion. In the Armed Forces, even a small error in a written order can lead to serious consequences. Therefore, recruits are trained not only in weapons handling and physical fitness but also in reading comprehension, grammar, and vocabulary. This combination of skills ensures that every soldier, regardless of his specific duty, can perform his responsibilities efficiently and accurately.\r\n\r\nWhat could happen because of an error in a written order, as per the passage?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The passage explicitly states that even a small error in a written order can lead to serious consequences.', NULL, NULL),
(803996, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Read the passage and answer the question that follows.\r\n\r\nGood communication skills are essential for every soldier, especially those working in administrative roles such as clerks and store keepers. Clear written and spoken English helps in maintaining accurate records, writing reports, and communicating instructions without confusion. In the Armed Forces, even a small error in a written order can lead to serious consequences. Therefore, recruits are trained not only in weapons handling and physical fitness but also in reading comprehension, grammar, and vocabulary. This combination of skills ensures that every soldier, regardless of his specific duty, can perform his responsibilities efficiently and accurately.\r\n\r\nBesides weapons handling and physical fitness, what else are recruits trained in, according to the passage?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The passage states that recruits are also trained in reading comprehension, grammar, and vocabulary alongside physical training.', NULL, NULL),
(803997, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Read the passage and answer the question that follows.\r\n\r\nRavi had always dreamed of joining the Indian Army since he was a young boy in his village. Every morning, he would run five kilometres before school to build his stamina. His father, a retired soldier, encouraged him to study hard alongside his physical training, reminding him that the entrance examination tested not just fitness but also mathematics, general knowledge, and English. Ravi took this advice seriously and spent two hours daily improving his vocabulary and grammar. When the recruitment rally was finally announced in his district, Ravi felt both nervous and excited. He knew that years of disciplined preparation had brought him to this crucial moment in his life.\r\n\r\nWhat did Ravi do every morning to build his stamina?', '1', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The passage states that Ravi would run five kilometres before school every morning to build his stamina.', NULL, NULL),
(803998, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Read the passage and answer the question that follows.\r\n\r\nRavi had always dreamed of joining the Indian Army since he was a young boy in his village. Every morning, he would run five kilometres before school to build his stamina. His father, a retired soldier, encouraged him to study hard alongside his physical training, reminding him that the entrance examination tested not just fitness but also mathematics, general knowledge, and English. Ravi took this advice seriously and spent two hours daily improving his vocabulary and grammar. When the recruitment rally was finally announced in his district, Ravi felt both nervous and excited. He knew that years of disciplined preparation had brought him to this crucial moment in his life.\r\n\r\nWho encouraged Ravi to study alongside his physical training?', '2', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The passage mentions that Ravi\'s father, a retired soldier, encouraged him to study hard alongside physical training.', NULL, NULL),
(803999, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Read the passage and answer the question that follows.\r\n\r\nRavi had always dreamed of joining the Indian Army since he was a young boy in his village. Every morning, he would run five kilometres before school to build his stamina. His father, a retired soldier, encouraged him to study hard alongside his physical training, reminding him that the entrance examination tested not just fitness but also mathematics, general knowledge, and English. Ravi took this advice seriously and spent two hours daily improving his vocabulary and grammar. When the recruitment rally was finally announced in his district, Ravi felt both nervous and excited. He knew that years of disciplined preparation had brought him to this crucial moment in his life.\r\n\r\nAccording to the passage, what subjects does the entrance examination test besides fitness?', '3', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Medium', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The passage states that the entrance examination tested fitness as well as mathematics, general knowledge, and English.', NULL, NULL),
(804000, 517, NULL, NULL, 0, '[General English] Read the passage and answer the question that follows.\r\n\r\nRavi had always dreamed of joining the Indian Army since he was a young boy in his village. Every morning, he would run five kilometres before school to build his stamina. His father, a retired soldier, encouraged him to study hard alongside his physical training, reminding him that the entrance examination tested not just fitness but also mathematics, general knowledge, and English. Ravi took this advice seriously and spent two hours daily improving his vocabulary and grammar. When the recruitment rally was finally announced in his district, Ravi felt both nervous and excited. He knew that years of disciplined preparation had brought him to this crucial moment in his life.\r\n\r\nHow did Ravi feel when the recruitment rally was finally announced?', '4', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'N', 'Easy', 'Y', 'N', NULL, NULL, 'MCQ', 4, 'The passage states that Ravi felt both nervous and excited when the recruitment rally was announced in his district.', NULL, NULL);
